{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition","id":1504062,"title":"So I'm currently reading the 2nd Edition...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-28T11:57:59-08:00","id":1504062,"title":"So I'm currently reading the 2nd Edition...","content":"...And there's no AKD or Ashewood Abbey in the core book.<br /> What's the reason for these changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T12:03:54-08:00","id":1504065,"title":"","content":"They're actually somewhat present in basic mechanical form in the book: they're the examples used in the Storytelling chapter for the guidelines for creating compacts and conspiracies, including 2e Status benefits for both organizations and the rules for two sample Relics.<br /> <br /> There was some conversation during development on whether or not to deemphasize Ashwood Abbey as an up-front core example of player character behavior. I'm not as familiar with the decision to sideline the Aegis Kai Doru, aside from the general need to free up word count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T12:08:28-08:00","id":1504066,"title":"","content":"Perhaps there could've been more emphasis made on the 'hunting the most dangerous game' and 'occult socialite' aspects of the Abbey and less on the ''''parties''''.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T14:52:02-08:00","id":1504074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1504066#post1504066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps there could've been more emphasis made on the 'hunting the most dangerous game' and 'occult socialite' aspects of the Abbey and less on the ''''parties''''.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing of the matter is that the general approach the Abbey, hunting monsters because it's fun, was it's thematic point, and while hunting the most dangerous game or being an occult socialite can play into that, neither can stack up to that tentpole-particularly given how in being so, the Abbey reflects the very thing people are doing when they play Hunter: the Vigil. That said, the concensus was against Abbey, and they wanted room for a new compact, so it got relegated to being an example.<br /> <br /> While we know the goal was to show off a new conspiracy with the new edition and that space issues meant that another conspiracy would take the bullet, it's never been precisely explained why it was Aegis Kai Doru that took it (I mean, the other most likely candidate were the Ascending Ones, and I'm a bigger AO fan than an AKD fan, so I'm not complaining), but if I had to speculate a reason, I would wager that they wanted to have a longer time to workshop making the relic answer to the sacred prey of mages and werewolves work more fully and completely, which had a handy side benefit of downplaying arguments about Hunter's relationship with Mage Second Edition around release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-28-2023, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T16:59:00-08:00","id":1504230,"title":"","content":"Well, the upcoming Tending the Fire (the 2e Companion book) was stated to contain both the Abbey and the AKD with full writeups, so we are going to get them when he book will come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T15:08:05-08:00","id":1504494,"title":"","content":"Who are the AKD? White Wolf Wiki seems to have nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T15:11:22-08:00","id":1504495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1504494#post1504494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who are the AKD? White Wolf Wiki seems to have nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aegis Kai Doru. You know, the relic maniacs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T15:13:53-08:00","id":1504496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1504494#post1504494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who are the AKD? White Wolf Wiki seems to have nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aegis Kai Doru, a Greco-Roman heritaged organization of would-be Indiana Jones and Achilles who gather Relics to bring to bear against their sacred enemies of mages and werewolves, as well as other enemies who otherwise interfere with their secret goal of rebuilding the world to it's pre-lapserian glory. Also they like labyrinths and severed heads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T15:22:24-08:00","id":1504499,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a>, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-09T11:14:32-08:00","id":1504959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1504230#post1504230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the upcoming Tending the Fire (the 2e Companion book) was stated to contain both the Abbey and the AKD with full writeups, so we are going to get them when he book will come out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear it. I thought the absence of Ashwood Abbey from the Core was one of the many weaknesses of Hunter Second Edition compared to First Edition. I thought Ashwood Abbey did something quite key in first edition - they made it clear that Hunters are not the good guys. The desire to find things that aren't human and kill them is not a healthy one, and Ashwood Abbey exposed this more clearly than any of the other compacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T16:21:17-07:00","id":1513578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1504959#post1504959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Glad to hear it. I thought the absence of Ashwood Abbey from the Core was one of the many weaknesses of Hunter Second Edition compared to First Edition. I thought Ashwood Abbey did something quite key in first edition - they made it clear that Hunters are not the good guys. The desire to find things that aren't human and kill them is not a healthy one, and Ashwood Abbey exposed this more clearly than any of the other compacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I think that this is one of the biggest problems with Hunter: Not simply that &quot;hunters aren't the good guys&quot;, but that Hunters are by and large evil. The only Conspiracies that aren't objectively evil are the Council of Bones and the Lucifuge, and the Lucifuge are only not evil on an individual basis. I <i>guess</i> you could say the Ascending Ones aren't evil, but they are also drug dealers.<br /> Meanwhile over in Compacts the first one presented is Christian fundamentalists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T18:15:33-07:00","id":1513589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1513578#post1513578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I think that this is one of the biggest problems with Hunter: Not simply that &quot;hunters aren't the good guys&quot;, but that Hunters are by and large evil. The only Conspiracies that aren't objectively evil are the Council of Bones and the Lucifuge, and the Lucifuge are only not evil on an individual basis. I <i>guess</i> you could say the Ascending Ones aren't evil, but they are also drug dealers.<br /> Meanwhile over in Compacts the first one presented is Christian fundamentalists.</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels wildly reductive.<br /> <br /> The keyword to Conspiracies is &quot;compromise&quot;, which on the one hand means, yes, there's <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268660#post1268660\">a lot of monsters</a> at the top, and a lot of their action is definitely suspect, but on the other hand also means reaching a equitable middle ground on a lot of different fronts, which often means finding ways to work out where the alternatives are just out and out conflict.<br /> <br /> Like, I am the first person to point out how Hutners are not good guys, but to just put things into perspective, let's go through our list:<br /> <br /> Task Force: Valkyrie's dedication to the support and enforcement of the various Masquerades is useful when you remember that magic in the world of Chronicles is inherently damaging to the psychology of humanity, and that by maintaining the divide, it maintains a lot of the mental and physical health of both human and monstrous communities, and is a big support in helping more reasonable monstrous communities curtail the more extreme elements of monsters.<br /> <br /> The Malleus Maleficarum's dedication against vampires, demons, and mages, however warped the motivation can be, does mean that there is a targeted pressure against some of the most exploitative monsters out there, particularly since those are the ones that can damage a person's sense of self and psyche the most, and thus ensure that debilitating habits, addictions, and patterns of behavior are kept at least to the limtis of human management, and correspondingly encourage monsters to rely on dehumanizing tactics less than they might otherwise, and thus have less of their own problems eroding their own humanity.<br /> <br /> The CHeiron Group is just plain evil, but their practice proves that there is a whole world of medical and scientific advances to be discovered that could do a lot to improve the health and wellbeing of various kinds of communities, and while ultimately you'd still want to have more ethical and humane actors than extra-dimensional capitalists, they have already proven a host of wonder treatments and procedures that could not only change the standard of life for humans, but for monsters as well.<br /> <br /> The Aegis Kai Doru's crusade helps to combat against two of the most interested parties of the supernatural community in shaping regions to their own interests and counter to those of the people living there, and meanwhile their efforts to collect potentially harmful tools, understand them, and finding careful and safe application of the safer and more usable of them can end up doing a lot of good in the communities they operate. For the monsters, in creates a pressure to work more with the communities they're trying to shape and meet half way to better hide among them, and again that encourages more connectivity to their own humanity.<br /> <br /> The Ascending Ones, as a very old and proven institution, is a reliable institution for parties to reach out to for arranging peaceful and equitable compromises, between monstrous comunities, human communities, and between those two, and in providing backup to any coalition of actors who would wildly hurt a community. Their practice in elixirs also means that they have a wide a thriving pharmaceutrical background that can support the communities they're in, and those drug dealers (Who aren't inherently evil, let's note) allows for those to move more freely than they might in a regulated market, and for cheaper prices than they might otherwise be-and those drug dealers are also a very useful immediate response emergencies, which goes doubly useful in communities that are neglected by official organizations, and as final point, the over all economic strata of the three branches also means there's a lot more economic flow generated because of them.<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge are institutionally one of the most empathetic organizations out there, with any of their agents predisposed to help people dealing with struggling with their metaphorical demons, and are also the forefront actors against the most inhumane and uncaring monster sets out there, reining in the worst ruiners of human lives.<br /> <br /> The Knights of Saint George may actively serve the Abyss, but they do it in the interests of keeping the Abyss out of the world, and in so doing apply pressure to a monster that is all too keen to abandon careful and considerate application of their powers.<br /> <br /> The Les Mysteres do a lot to help maintain a healthy spiritual balance in the communities they participate in, and very vitally can provide a means for spirits to sustain themselves without neccesarily allowing them to go into excess, and thus are a powerful buffer their manipulations as well, and can provide pressures on werewolves to be mindful of their impact on spiritual communities as well.<br /> <br /> The Cainite Heresy are a bunch of fucks*, but their presence is a very solid reason for vampires to not give into excesses, control the damage they inflict on their victims, and with that possibly even have more reason to reflect on that humanity.<br /> <br /> The Vanguard Serial Crimes Unit is very good at rooting out what are often the most damaging and toxic elements of their communities, and their need to act in accordance to the law (in theory) allows for moments of possible mercy that might not otherwise be afforded.<br /> <br /> The Feast of Shulpae are a very effective deterrent towards carelessly and thoughtlessly trying to build cult activity, and can be an effective binder against the most egrigious of a class of monster whose carelessness and thoughtlessness on the whole can devastate regions, and all while still giving some due diligence to the nature of those beings, for whatever that's worth.<br /> <br /> The Knights of Saint Adrian are a bunch of fucks*, but their presence in the cultures of transience, which are much more vulnerable, provides a mesaure of defense, and their targets are often reality terrorists who are often willing to accept more devastating damage to reality.<br /> <br /> And the Merrick Insittue are a bunch of kids taking down a corrupt agency that is otherwise being constantly shielded by any number of interested parties, while also being among some of the most effective actors against one of the most adaptable monsters out there, and both by being-as-warning-of-consequence and action-as-pressure encourage more humanity in them.<br /> <br /> And by contrast-I actually don't know if I'm supposed to take the first compact being (apocalyptic) Christian Fundamentalists as a positve or a negative, so to immediately counter-play that, they are also (apocalyptic) Christian Fundamentalists.****<br /> <br /> Now, does any of that make any of those good guys? Fuck no, one of them is <i>still</i> the FBI**. With the exception of the Merrick Institute (because it's hard to really take a bunch of kids to task), every single one of them have wildly fucky attitudes and actions-but to say they're flat out evil ignores that they do, in fact, do good-maybe not what everyone can agree on as good, but again, that's kind of the point. THey're <i>complicated</i>, in a game where one of the points is that what can often seem like a completely black and white affair is instead more complicated than that. They engage with monstrosity, but then again, so does everyone else in Chronicles, and there's real humanity that is often engaged through that as well, even as it just as often leads to greater monstrosity.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hunters aren't the good guys&quot; isn't a refrain of mine because Hunters are, consequentially, &quot;the bad guys&quot;. Hunters are, like everything else in Chronicles, people, and people are wild, weird, varied, and not easily boxed. That's not to say there aren't good people, and that there aren't bad people, but at the end of the day, peoples is peoples.<br /> <br /> *even though I weirdly love them.<br /> **Well, First Edition wise, anyways***<br /> ***And if you don't think the FBI aren't monsters, Hoo boy.<br /> ****And just so I'm clear, I'm not fan of Christian fundamentalists....which is not to say they are, in my book, an unalloyed evil. To solidly class them as a net evil is to have an incomplete image of them, even if I still take them to task on the whole for their net negative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-01-2023, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T23:26:05-07:00","id":1513608,"title":"","content":"My issue is not that the orgs are compromised. The Lucifuge is compromised and they're the most morally good Conspiracy.<br /> The issue is that the organizations are evil. They're cops and Christian fundamentalist premillennial dispensationalists and the FBI and a morally reprehensible pharmaceutical company's paramility murder squad. Hunter orgs don't have to be evil.<br /> <br /> So many orgs treat moral greyness as just being evil. The Lucifuge, Ascending Ones, Network Zero, SWORN, Null Mysteriis, Council of Bones, and The Union (when they aren't written as being friendly with law enforcement, the enemy of the working class) from the corebook are all varying shades of morally grey <i>and/</i><i>or</i> compromised, and yet they're organizations that don't come off as antagonists. I'm not as well up on the expanded orgs, but you don't need a group to be morally reprehensible or based on actual real world groups like fundamentalists or the fucking Hong Kong police (written while they were brutalizing protesters).<br /> <br /> I also don't see how telling me what role they could facilitate in the other gamelines really accomplishes. That the Faithful of Shulpae make a good Mummy antagonist doesn't really mean anything when I'm talking about how they function as Hunter <i>pro</i>tagonists. The type of Hunter that goes around murdering innocent supernaturals who haven't done anything harmful is generally agreed upon as a bad character type who shouldn't be a player character. Even CW's Supernatural portrayed such characters as villains, and that's a show where anything supernatural is repeatedly proven to be objectively evil. Yet that's the sort of character that Faithful and Cheiron agents facilitate. Even the Conspiracy that I made, the Hunters are morally grey and even more than usual openly consorting with monsters, but they're also not cannibal serial killers, Pinkertons with psychic powers, believers in turn of the century racial pseudoscience, or <i>The Catholic Church</i>'s secret killers. The problem with the Malleus is not that Ambrogio Baudolino is a ghoul. The problem is that they're the Vatican's monster hunters. The problem with Taskforce: VALKYRIE is not that they're funded by vampires, the problem is that they're the US Military. The problem with Cheiron is not that they're run by space aliens, it's that they're run by people who think making medicine cost an arm and a leg is good.<br /> <br /> The problem is that no amount of &quot;these specific people are nice and good&quot; can make me ignore the real world groups these things are based on, like fundamentalist churches or the fucking police.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Vanguard Serial Crimes Unit is very good at rooting out what are often the most damaging and toxic elements of their communities, and their need to act in accordance to the law (in theory) allows for moments of possible mercy that might not otherwise be afforded. </div> </div> </div>The issue here is that we already know what &quot;acting in accordance to the law&quot; doesn't mean anything in the real world, why would it mean anything in the Chronicles of Darkness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T03:28:47-07:00","id":1513625,"title":"","content":"Okay, that clarifies on those points, and let's be clear-I am not on the side of the police, Christian fundamentalists, exploitative hyper capatilist pharmaceutical and medical organizations, etc., etc., and Hunter is definitely a lens to examine all of that.<br /> <br /> But, and this is the important part, in the context of a game franchise <i>about monsters</i> in a gameline that is about the <i>monstrosity of humanity </i>in direct pursuit of <i>acting against monstrosity</i>, and recognizing the humanity that exist in that monstrosity, it centralizes on the duality of the problem-one, that opposition towards building better worlds are still human, and two, that humanity doesn't excuse their strife.<br /> <br /> The people who make up these systemic evils are people, like anyone else, and are motivated a lot of the banal things that everyone participates in. If we can play Vampire with an expectation that we're to find humanity in a creature who sucks blood, addicts people to their personages, and warp communities, then Hunter does the same with FBI agents. To deny that humanity is to commit to the same sin of Hunters in general, taking against monsters of the night without accounting for their humanity, and that very rapidly escalates to slasherdom as people who do that basically begin to self-justify excess power being exercised.<br /> <br /> But, in the same way that it draws a line between their humanity, Hunter draws a line between the strife committed by the vampire and the FBI agent-and have no doubts about it, the games still does not deny the damage a vampire commits, and pretty well makes the argument that even the best intentioned of them is still a long term cost on any given community. That analogy cuts both ways-just because the FBI is made up of people does not stop the FBI from being a harmful organization that, at the end of the day, needs something done about it. Not doing something about either encourages a systemic rot that will only get worse the less is done.<br /> <br /> What Hunter asks is to balance the two factors, and it's conclusion is a very good lesson for progressives trying to build better worlds, particularly as the violence to push for that better world only continues to escalate-the need to violence corruption (however you go about it) cannot deny the humanity of that corruption if it wants to avoid becoming more of the same. Hunters are victims of the creatures of the night, and their crusade is often an immediate response to that harm inflicted, an emotional reaction that is useful <i>if used correctly</i>.<br /> <br /> The hall mark of a lot of anti-progressive movements and institutionalization is, quite frankly, hatred against the perceived non-normal, and that hatred is not going to handled with clean white gloves-the system needs to be violenced. But if we're going to avoid Nietzschean cliches in dealing with that, then that violence cannot also dehumanize the opposition. It has to deal with the injustice, it has to deal with the corruption, but it also has to recognize the humanity of the people that is interwoven with that. There needs to be anger, fury, determination, a coldness to act and get through, but it also demands empathy, kindness, understanding. And balancing those two is REALLY HARD, and it's not an even distribution at all times. It's going to be case by case, handling the building brick-by-brick, moment-by-moment, and that's going to have missteps and errors and costs. That's why the whole damn thing is so damn hard, even disregarding the complete imbalance of it all*.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I still think it's a bit reductive. It's not untrue, mind you, but it's definitely not the whole picture.<br /> <br /> And I say this as someone who recognized the dangers in the political situation in their country because I recognized that &quot;Hey, the Union's kind of fucked up actually.&quot; That thought is a very significant kickstarter to my being the leftist I am today.<br /> <br /> *like hell, there's another useful metaphor-Hunters, because they lack power, aren't very often in a position to offer meaningful mercy, and in fact have to rely on excessive violence to make a difference, but by that very fact, the excessive violence is an act that risks dehumanizing the actors, and there's no real way around that-but by acknowledging it advance, it can be planned and worked around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T15:36:35-07:00","id":1513974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1513608#post1513608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is that the organizations are evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't previously thought too much about this for Hunter specifically, but on reflection, I wonder how playable many of the Hunter conspiracies actually are. For example, how many people have actually done a Hunter game where everyone works for Cheiron? Cheiron's interesting as a setting element, but they wouldn't be my first, second or third choice of conspiracy for a Hunter PC, and I think you'd need a pretty specific mindset to have fun with a character who's internal organs are owned by their employer.<br /> And none of this means that Cheiron shouldn't be in the game or anything, but they're presented as a sample organization that player characters are theoretically expected to join and I'm not sure how useful they actually are for that purpose, rather than as a setting element, source of dark jokes, or supplier of antagonists for monsters and indie hunters alike.<br /> Although that's less because I think they're evil and more because they don't strike me as much fun to actually play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T00:17:50-07:00","id":1513991,"title":"","content":"[Ignore this]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-07-2023, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T00:19:59-07:00","id":1513992,"title":"","content":"(I think I broke something trying to put a link in a quote name; if a mod sees the other post just delete it don't approve it, it's broken)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1513625#post1513625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in the context of a game franchise <i>about monsters</i> in a gameline that is about the <i>monstrosity of humanity </i>in direct pursuit of <i>acting against monstrosity</i>, and recognizing the humanity that exist in that monstrosity, it centralizes on the duality of the problem-one, that opposition towards building better worlds are still human, and two, that humanity doesn't excuse their strife.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't really agree that your Orgs need to be evil to be have the &quot;he who fights monsters&quot; theme. I mean, there are plenty that aren't monsters.<br /> I actually recently <a href=\"https://esperism.notion.site/Hunter-Orgs-d028281a23184e7da94bc067de473581?pvs=4\" target=\"_blank\">made a list</a>.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunters are victims of the creatures of the night, and their crusade is often an immediate response to that harm inflicted, an emotional reaction that is useful <i>if used correctly</i>.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I mean, Cheiron is not made up of victims. Taskforce VALKYRIE is not made up of victims. Again, I don't think the <i>organization</i> needs to be evil just to have Hunters that do morally questionable acts. It's not like the Courts or Orders are made up of groups that are overtly evil. Even the Guardians aren't <i>completely</i> evil and going around killing monsters to make boner pills and high price cancer treatment.<br /> <br /> I also think that what the book does downplay is the harm the <i>FBI</i> commits. And at the end of the day every one of the FBI's people\u2014or VALKYRIE's or Cheiron's or the Long Night's or the Hunt Club's\u2014is someone who is actively choosing to do evil. And why would I want to play someone like that, unless I'm explicitly choosing to play an evil person? Why should they be presented as the player options instead of being kept for the Antagonist section like the Pure and the Seers and Belial's Brood? Why not make groups that are actually noble but flawed? Again, those are already some of the best Orgs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hadn't previously thought too much about this for Hunter specifically, but on reflection, I wonder how playable many of the Hunter conspiracies actually are. [...] Although that's less because I think they're evil and more because they don't strike me as much fun to actually play.</div> </div> </div> </div>A separate but tangential issue that plagues the gameline as well. Like, &quot;the guys who pretty much only hunt werewolves and do it out of sport&quot; don't really even seem like they'd be interesting to play. Half the orgs feel like set dressing instead of things you want to play. The Talbot Group for instance. It even says they hire other Hunters to capture werewolves for them.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T15:01:35-07:00","id":1514056,"title":"","content":"I dont know man, your list is highly subjective and ironically ignores any nuance to the orgs. And the books do tend to sure orgs in a grey light, while the individuals are, more often than not, portrayed as much more relatable and I'd claim a better light. I don't see an issue with a law force group being portrayed in something other than an evil light. I think that paints a rather shallow picture of a rather complicated moral area. Seriously, I'd say second edition did a lot more toward making the compacts and conspiracies look like good guys.<br /> <br /> The position on talbot group is just an opinion of yours. They present another type of hunt. One of misplaced good intentions and trying to maintain a monster in a way just not meant for it. I had a hell of a lot of fun doing an episodic campaign where we were the talbot group. We talked to the patients, followed up on spirit rumors, and even had to try and subdue an enraged patient.<br /> <br /> As for the mage comparison...well, just like changelings people white wash the hell out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T10:31:33-07:00","id":1514115,"title":"","content":"I don't see anything in 2e that makes the worse Orgs look like good guys. There are a few more examples of &quot;you're pressganged&quot;. And the threat of the world being overrun by supernaturals. That doesn't really make them less as bad as the monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T15:00:33-07:00","id":1514135,"title":"","content":"The vast majority of example characters are direct victims of the supernatural, and the threat of the world being taken by the supernatural is a genuine threat. In fact, the very concept of hunters is why many if not all the monsters accept some variation of a masquerade. Also, all the gamelines have example characters that range from very sympathetic to cruel monsters in all ways. <br /> <br /> Is the issue that you want hunters to be outright heroes in terms of organizations? Because that's just not possible. All groups have problems, whether or not it carries saints within them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T15:21:43-07:00","id":1514137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514135#post1514135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that's just not possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of Hunter orgs that aren't evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T18:02:11-07:00","id":1514150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514137#post1514137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of Hunter orgs that aren't evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have the bandwidth to give the response I want to right now, so in the mean time, I'm going to borrow from Lindsay Ellis's words on the subject of Disney pretending to be woke.<br /> <br /> &quot;<a href=\"https://youtu.be/xU1ffHa47YY?t=1416\" target=\"_blank\">You have declared the thing problematic. Yeah, great. Good for you. In the words of Alan Arkin,<br /> <br /> So?</a>&quot;<br /> <br /> Like's, starting with &quot;these things are evil&quot; is a bad starting point that's clearly not understanding both Hunter's themes and Chronicles' themes in general, but if we must use it, I must then ask if you have even bothered to actually ask yourself why they did that in the first place, because the complaint falls apart with any serious interrogation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-07-2023, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T20:59:06-07:00","id":1514157,"title":"","content":"I mean the Pretty Knights Aspel got put girls in danger to get good Matiral for their Manga, and they work within the idol industry, which<br /> <br /> <br /> Is bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T22:08:28-07:00","id":1514160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514137#post1514137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of Hunter orgs that aren't evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>All are flawed though. Even the aforementioned talbot group is doing far more harm than good to its patients.<br /> <br /> And doesn't that statement contradict your whole argument?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T22:30:23-07:00","id":1514165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514150#post1514150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like's, starting with &quot;these things are evil&quot; is a bad starting point that's clearly not understanding both Hunter's themes and Chronicles' themes in general, but if we must use it, I must then ask if you have even bothered to actually ask yourself why they did that in the first place, because the complaint falls apart with any serious interrogation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I know why they did it. You have already explained what you see as the core themes and why you feel that these evil orgs being intended for players is not an issue. I've heard you. Hearing you is not the problem, the problem is that I simply disagree. This isn't simply that I've declared the thing problematic. I have pointed out that making the protagonist factions so evil that they are actually villains of <i>other groups within the gameline</i> is not really necessary for a theme of doing bad things to fight the monsters. There are plenty of orgs that act as counter examples, and the game would not actually suffer all that much\u2014if at all\u2014if more of there were more Orgs like the Union, Network Zero, Lucifuge, the Ascending Ones, or even the Aegis Kai Doru, and things like Taskforce VALKYRIE or Cheiron were in the Antagonist section.<br /> <br /> It's not like my argument is that Hunter orgs should all be squeaky clean and filled with only nice people of Integrity 7. As Cross-a-way points out, my own Hunter Conspiracy isn't exactly untarnished. Not sure where the idol bit comes from (they do cosplay, not idol work), but they have their own propaganda wing. Hell, <i>two</i> of the factions are essentially propaganda wings. And the things they work with are not all your friendly Fairest Playmate Spring Courtier who just wants everyone to be happy. Hell, I even give the implication that they will work with <i>True Fae</i>, so long as they aren't overtly hostile.<br /> <br /> I don't think the setting is worse for having Taskforce VALKYRIE. Hell, I'm planning a Taskforce VALKYRIE game at the moment. Albeit one where the players are made as Horrors and they're armed with bomb collars. Cheiron and VALKYRIE existing help me know what my Deviant is on the run from. I just think that maybe starting the book by saying &quot;anyway here's some apocalypse cultists who believe the world is filled with monsters, they're totally different from the real life apocalypse cultists who believe the world is filled with monsters&quot; is maybe not great. I think the game is worse for <i>that</i>. I think that the game is worse for forcing players to either choose to work for groups that they find evil and come up with a reason their player character isn't evil or to simply never play a Tier 2 or 3 game and miss out on the best part (the cool powers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514160#post1514160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All are flawed though. Even the aforementioned talbot group is doing far more harm than good to its patients.<br /> <br /> And doesn't that statement contradict your whole argument?</div> </div> </div> </div>My argument is that Hunter orgs do not need to have a handbook that labels anything supernatural as a &quot;Reality Deviant&quot; or a write up all about which monsters get made into boner pills to be interesting or morally complex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-08-2023, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T15:00:07-07:00","id":1514245,"title":"","content":"Again, I'm at work and just don't have the energy to deconstruct how the emphasis on evil is indicative of not engaging with Hunter's themes, or Chronicles's themes on the whole, for whatever reason, but I do want at least point more in the direction of what my issue is than an admittedly glib response will do, so to that end, I'm gonn post a bit from one scrapped response that I feel still really worked well. <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, Cheiron is not made up of victims. Taskforce VALKYRIE is not made up of victims. </div> </div> </div>You're starting from a top down perspective that is not helping you to understand the picture Hunter is painting.<br /> <br /> The books demonstrate time and again that engagement with the supernatural is not a thing that people casually do for almost any given reason, given that the supernatural in all of it's forms its actively psychologically and spiritually stressful and damaging-most people's responses are to try and keep themselves as distant from the supernatural as they can after one or two exceptional intrustions. Mortal investigators from the Chronicles corebook are often individuals who are in the middle of one of those exceptional intrusions and are written with a general understanding that most of them will go back to not looking too closely at the shadows once a chronicle is over, with a rare few exceptions diving deeper to understand it better to better interact with it (or, more realistically, be even better at not engaging with it, or at least not without protections).<br /> <br /> The sort of person who becomes a hunter, a person who not only interacts and investigates the supernatural but actively work to harm in it a variety of ways in the name of a variety of causes and reasons, is an expectation above and beyond that, and the general root of that is a resolution against the harm they dealt with in their one or two exceptional experiences with the supernatural. Hunter: the Vigil First Edition's corebook is pretty upfront and explicit about that, pretty well opening it's world building chapter at the start of the book with &quot;Yeah, pretty much every hunter is a victim of supernatural violence of some sort.&quot;<br /> <br /> So if you wanted to provide a fuller line, a non-reductive line with this, it might go something like &quot;The Field Projects Division of the Cheiron Group and Task Force: Valkyrie are not, institutionally, victims in any meaningful sense, but there are things about them that are attractive to victims of supernatural violence that lead to making up a lot of those organizations with those victims.&quot;\u200b <hr />And as addendum to that, it's in that attraction that more of the overall point is found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-08-2023, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T17:16:14-07:00","id":1514254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514165#post1514165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I know why they did it. You have already explained what you see as the core themes and why you feel that these evil orgs being intended for players is not an issue. I've heard you. Hearing you is not the problem, the problem is that I simply disagree. This isn't simply that I've declared the thing problematic. I have pointed out that making the protagonist factions so evil that they are actually villains of <i>other groups within the gameline</i> is not really necessary for a theme of doing bad things to fight the monsters. There are plenty of orgs that act as counter examples, and the game would not actually suffer all that much\u2014if at all\u2014if more of there were more Orgs like the Union, Network Zero, Lucifuge, the Ascending Ones, or even the Aegis Kai Doru, and things like Taskforce VALKYRIE or Cheiron were in the Antagonist section.<br /> <br /> It's not like my argument is that Hunter orgs should all be squeaky clean and filled with only nice people of Integrity 7. As Cross-a-way points out, my own Hunter Conspiracy isn't exactly untarnished. Not sure where the idol bit comes from (they do cosplay, not idol work), but they have their own propaganda wing. Hell, <i>two</i> of the factions are essentially propaganda wings. And the things they work with are not all your friendly Fairest Playmate Spring Courtier who just wants everyone to be happy. Hell, I even give the implication that they will work with <i>True Fae</i>, so long as they aren't overtly hostile.<br /> <br /> I don't think the setting is worse for having Taskforce VALKYRIE. Hell, I'm planning a Taskforce VALKYRIE game at the moment. Albeit one where the players are made as Horrors and they're armed with bomb collars. Cheiron and VALKYRIE existing help me know what my Deviant is on the run from. I just think that maybe starting the book by saying &quot;anyway here's some apocalypse cultists who believe the world is filled with monsters, they're totally different from the real life apocalypse cultists who believe the world is filled with monsters&quot; is maybe not great. I think the game is worse for <i>that</i>. I think that the game is worse for forcing players to either choose to work for groups that they find evil and come up with a reason their player character isn't evil or to simply never play a Tier 2 or 3 game and miss out on the best part (the cool powers).<br /> <br /> My argument is that Hunter orgs do not need to have a handbook that labels anything supernatural as a &quot;Reality Deviant&quot; or a write up all about which monsters get made into boner pills to be interesting or morally complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that argument is literally just strawmanning the organizations, as if the chieron group doesn't also make life saving medicines. And hunter orgs don't need handbooks saying that. It's unique to only one group and I don't see the problem with it. Like honestly I dont","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T16:03:16-07:00","id":1514349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514165#post1514165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\\There are plenty of orgs that act as counter examples, and the game would not actually suffer all that much\u2014if at all\u2014if more of there were more Orgs like the Union, Network Zero, Lucifuge, the Ascending Ones, or even the Aegis Kai Doru, and things like Taskforce VALKYRIE or Cheiron were in the Antagonist section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, a canon antagonist military-industrial faction like MJ12 from Delta Green or the Black Chamber from the Laundry Files would have been freaking cool. Technically Hunter-orgs but suffering from a terminal case of regulatory capture.<br /> <br /> Aspel, I think you've got a valid point, anyway. I did notice after your first post that I was glossing over the fucking Long Night or Ashwood Abbey in my own mental list of Hunter orgs. I... really don't know what you're supposed to do with them EXCEPT to present them as a really tempting alternate opponent for your players to shoot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","user":"Niknokk","date":". 06-09-2023, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T19:00:22-07:00","id":1514379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514349#post1514349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspel, I think you've got a valid point, anyway. I did notice after your first post that I was glossing over the fucking Long Night or Ashwood Abbey in my own mental list of Hunter orgs. I... really don't know what you're supposed to do with them EXCEPT to present them as a really tempting alternate opponent for your players to shoot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, stuff like this falls apart when you stop hanging onto &quot;These organizations are evil by virtue of being attached to real world evil&quot; and instead engage with the humanity versus monstrosity argument Chronicles has and apply that lens, as Hunter does, to real world organizations. Understanding that hunters are monsters and that monsters is a diverse phrase with a lot of meanings which pretty well translates monstrosity into circumstances, then it becomes pretty easy to understand the Long Night.<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey deserves a particular mention, because while that same &quot;actually engaging with the themes and narrative of the game&quot; clears them up a lot, Ashwood is also the most meta of the organizations, in that they are a bunch of people who gather together to hunt down monsters for fun* in the real world scenario where you and your friends gather together to hunt down monsters for fun-and if that gives you any pause, rest assured that pause is the issue that Abbey hunters also deal with.<br /> <br /> *and attempt to handle trauma in the way every other hunter does, I really need that post to be approved, damnit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T10:25:33-07:00","id":1514478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514349#post1514349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, a canon antagonist military-industrial faction like MJ12 from Delta Green or the Black Chamber from the Laundry Files would have been freaking cool. Technically Hunter-orgs but suffering from a terminal case of regulatory capture.<br /> <br /> Aspel, I think you've got a valid point, anyway. I did notice after your first post that I was glossing over the fucking Long Night or Ashwood Abbey in my own mental list of Hunter orgs. I... really don't know what you're supposed to do with them EXCEPT to present them as a really tempting alternate opponent for your players to shoot.</div> </div> </div> </div>If those organizations should only be antagonists, then all gamelines don't deserve to be protagonists, including most of the organizations in them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 06-10-2023, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T12:13:56-07:00","id":1514493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514379#post1514379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, stuff like this falls apart when you stop hanging onto &quot;These organizations are evil by virtue of being attached to real world evil&quot; and instead engage with the humanity versus monstrosity argument Chronicles has and apply that lens, as Hunter does, to real world organizations. Understanding that hunters are monsters and that monsters is a diverse phrase with a lot of meanings which pretty well translates monstrosity into circumstances, then it becomes pretty easy to understand the Long Night.<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey deserves a particular mention, because while that same &quot;actually engaging with the themes and narrative of the game&quot; clears them up a lot, Ashwood is also the most meta of the organizations, in that they are a bunch of people who gather together to hunt down monsters for fun* in the real world scenario where you and your friends gather together to hunt down monsters for fun-and if that gives you any pause, rest assured that pause is the issue that Abbey hunters also deal with.<br /> <br /> *and attempt to handle trauma in the way every other hunter does, I really need that post to be approved, damnit</div> </div> </div> </div>If we aren't careful, we can put ourselves in a bind where we either risk going way over player comfort levels in portraying a real-world evil, or we soft-pedal the real-world evil for the sake of making it playable, which is also uncomfortable. I don't think it's a terminal problem for Hunter, but I do think it's a sticking point that deserves to be taken seriously when someone has an issue with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T12:45:33-07:00","id":1514497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514493#post1514493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we aren't careful, we can put ourselves in a bind where we either risk going way over player comfort levels in portraying a real-world evil, or we soft-pedal the real-world evil for the sake of making it playable, which is also uncomfortable. I don't think it's a terminal problem for Hunter, but I do think it's a sticking point that deserves to be taken seriously when someone has an issue with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As if &quot;fictional evil&quot; isn't any worse? Corpses that turn you into a drug dependent sycophant tied to an abuser, living nightmares who's existence is to traumatize, and demons who manipulate people into predatory contracts are fine to play as because they *totally* don't reflect real world evils<br /> <br /> Or alchemical abominations who will treat people like shit and as goalposts being justified from following refinements? What about monster organizations which glorify war and conflict? Or see people as resources at best? Are we forgetting about mummies than their cults? You know, the kind of organization many real world people end up becoming victims to?<br /> <br /> Why are those fine to play as, but not a Christian group opposes to these monsters or a pharmaceutical company that makes medicines that can change your life for the better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 06-10-2023, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T14:38:42-07:00","id":1514513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514493#post1514493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we aren't careful, we can put ourselves in a bind where we either risk going way over player comfort levels in portraying a real-world evil, or we soft-pedal the real-world evil for the sake of making it playable, which is also uncomfortable. I don't think it's a terminal problem for Hunter, but I do think it's a sticking point that deserves to be taken seriously when someone has an issue with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aspel mentioned Deviant, which is convenient because the Devoted Companion just came out a couple months ago, addresses playing members of evil conspiracies who literally become more stable when they're powered by hate, and literally mentions in its systems for creating a conspiracy in-setting that the necessary Objectives are usually distasteful, unethical, or immoral; that vibe is not unique to Deviant.<br /> <br /> Conspiracies in Hunter are characterized as organized from the top down in contrast to the more regional bottom-up structure of a compact. If you look around at the rest of the franchise, you may notice that organizations that are <i>organizations</i> rather than localized expressions of a widespread philosophical system (a la werewolf tribes, Promethean Refinements, conventional changeling courts, etc) tend to be increasingly compromised with scale and power (see also krewes, Arisen cults, the Seers of the Throne, etc), to say nothing of cults of personality like those cultivated by vampires and demons and beasts.<br /> <br /> My primary beef with Hunter Second Edition has been its carrying forward of the tendency seen in Mortal Remains to treat the conspiracies as known quantities among their peers instead of mutually secretive groups like the name indicates, but the fact remains that hunter organizations above the level of a cell tend to infiltrate or manipulate unaffiliated cells in their orbit to take risks they don't want to take themselves \u2014 see the conversation with the Chevalier Th\u00e9l\u00e8me and his interviewer in the Horror Recognition Guide \u2014 and that, even without a Supernatural Potency stat to directly fill the role (Compact/Conspiracy Status comes the closest to proxying for it), long-established hunters implicitly have worn down their Integrity to a lower level and/or altered it through the Code, having gone through experiences that damage their ability to relate to people and carry on a life outside the Vigil; note that the Merciless Condition switches the circumstances in which a hunter hemorrhages Willpower from &quot;supernatural danger to a human being&quot; to &quot;a new monster's presence&quot; and switches the rewards for certain Willpower-risking situations from aligning with their Virtue to aligning with their Vice.<br /> <br /> These are long-running groups whose core membership is made up of and whose guiding principles are driven by people who are very likely to have seen and done things that have made them particularly ruthless and focused primarily on the pursuit of the supernatural in the name of humanity in the abstract or the concrete particular. Even without a connection to a large public-facing organization or profession with known issues, this is a category of people who instrumentalize other people (not uncommonly without their knowledge or consent) in the name of specific goals for approaching the supernatural in a setting where the supernatural is traumatic for the vast majority of people to encounter, including hunters, and that's part of why some of them help <i>hide</i> the supernatural from the public. I don't expect the fucking Men In Black to be morally blameless even without the indiscretions of the United States military, and I don't assign much in the way of special moral dimension to &quot;the Long Night believe the End Times are upon us and monsters walk the earth&quot; because that's their institutional mythology's in-universe justification for why a collection of church-basement Bible-study groups coordinate to hunt monsters.<br /> <br /> This is a setting that superficially resembles the world as we know it except with magic and monsters in the shadows, and when magic and monsters have and are sources of power that means the powerful have reason to be concerned with these subjects as things to have on their side and to fear being turned against them. The real-world evils of the Catholic Church are not the driving focus of the Malleus Maleficarum in a game where you are playing a witch-hunter sent to stake and extract a vampiric slumlord, for all that that mission exists to feed the addiction of a centuries-old ghoul placed highly in the Church.The fact that the Cheiron Group is an evil corporation whose main positive moral aspect is that the monsters it sends its Field Projects Division after may be doing harm to people is not meaningfully different from other conspiracies in the practical sense of &quot;if you belong to a hunter organization big and old and strong enough to give you cool magic powers, those tend to come with the obligations attendant to that structure and those obligations may wear on your independence and/or your scruples.&quot; The Union aren't even at that level of insitutional corruption, and their being majority Home First tells you all you need to know re: &quot;these are only 'good guys' in the sense that they have people they care about.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T11:19:10-07:00","id":1514586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514379#post1514379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, stuff like this falls apart when you stop hanging onto &quot;These organizations are evil by virtue of being attached to real world evil&quot; and instead engage with the humanity versus monstrosity argument Chronicles has and apply that lens, as Hunter does, to real world organizations. Understanding that hunters are monsters and that monsters is a diverse phrase with a lot of meanings which pretty well translates monstrosity into circumstances, then it becomes pretty easy to understand the Long Night.<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey deserves a particular mention, because while that same &quot;actually engaging with the themes and narrative of the game&quot; clears them up a lot, Ashwood is also the most meta of the organizations, in that they are a bunch of people who gather together to hunt down monsters for fun* in the real world scenario where you and your friends gather together to hunt down monsters for fun-and if that gives you any pause, rest assured that pause is the issue that Abbey hunters also deal with.<br /> <br /> *and attempt to handle trauma in the way every other hunter does, I really need that post to be approved, damnit</div> </div> </div> </div>The Abbey are increasingly depicted as serial rapists who don't care what they hunt and do it not because they were traumatized by the Supernatural but because it's fun and they're rich people. Ashwood Abbey doesn't go out and hunt monsters for fun because they enjoy a roleplaying game where you get to be heroic and kill the vampire that's preying on your community or hunt down the Beast of Gevaudan, they're doing it because they explicitly want to (often nonconsensually) engage in depraved sexual acts with the monster. Sometimes they even join it in doing horrible things. There is not really a &quot;oh, this is a dark lens upon you the player&quot; to be held up here unless your players are horrible people, but I'm going to assume most aren't.<br /> Hunters are not monsters. There is nothing about the corebook that really even implies that. Integrity is not Morality and the book goes out of it's way to draw an &quot;us&quot; vs &quot;them&quot; line in several places. Hunters are &quot;he who fights monsters should do well to not become a monster himself&quot;, but they don't start out as monsters. They *potentially* become monsters as a result of the things they experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514254#post1514254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that argument is literally just strawmanning the organizations, as if the chieron group doesn't also make life saving medicines. And hunter orgs don't need handbooks saying that. It's unique to only one group and I don't see the problem with it. Like honestly I dont</div> </div> </div> </div>Making lifesaving medicines that you also price gouge and make through murder is a bad thing. And this problem of &quot;they hunt monsters... and also eat babies!!!&quot; isn't unique to Cheiron.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514497#post1514497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As if &quot;fictional evil&quot; isn't any worse? Corpses that turn you into a drug dependent sycophant tied to an abuser, living nightmares who's existence is to traumatize, and demons who manipulate people into predatory contracts are fine to play as because they *totally* don't reflect real world evils<br /> <br /> Or alchemical abominations who will treat people like shit and as goalposts being justified from following refinements? What about monster organizations which glorify war and conflict? Or see people as resources at best? Are we forgetting about mummies than their cults? You know, the kind of organization many real world people end up becoming victims to?<br /> <br /> Why are those fine to play as, but not a Christian group opposes to these monsters or a pharmaceutical company that makes medicines that can change your life for the better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because those are treated as sympathetic within their own games. Not every vampire is spamming Dominate on everyone they meet and draining everyone to the last health. Not every Promethean is objectifying everyone they meet. I don't actually like or care about Mummy, so I can't really say anything in defense of that one. Those are fine to play as because you're taking extreme stereotypes of how someone could be evil as a member of those templates as opposed to simply letting them exist. Those are also <i>templates</i> you're stereotyping while I'm talking about <i>organizations.</i> You don't really have a choice in if you exist in the world as a Promethean or Vampire, you do have a choice to join an org. But the Ordo Dracul are evil and they're in the game about being a vampire, not the game about being a monster hunter. The Cheiron Group fits within the world of the game, but it doesn't fit the themes of responding to trauma.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> It is just baffling to me that people are essentially arguing that Hunter is somehow uniquely monstrous among the lines and the idea that maybe the overtly antagonistic orgs that are treated <i>in the Hunter book</i> as being exceptionally evil are not really good. Hunters are desperate people who become traumatized. None of the evil Orgs really facilitate that, because despite the arguments to the contrary, they are *not* evil as a result of supernatural trauma. They're evil because they want to make money or fuck monsters and don't even ostensibly care about the victims of themselves or the monsters.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not saying Hunter orgs have to be paragons of justice. I'm just saying that maybe they shouldn't be at the same level as the Vampires who slaughter homeless people just to experiment on them. No one is jonesing to make the Free Council or Spring Court more overtly evil. Why should the Hunter orgs be worse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-11-2023, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T12:03:12-07:00","id":1514597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514586#post1514586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abbey are increasingly depicted as serial rapists who don't care what they hunt and do it not because they were traumatized by the Supernatural but because it's fun and they're rich people. Ashwood Abbey doesn't go out and hunt monsters for fun because they enjoy a roleplaying game where you get to be heroic and kill the vampire that's preying on your community or hunt down the Beast of Gevaudan, they're doing it because they explicitly want to (often nonconsensually) engage in depraved sexual acts with the monster. Sometimes they even join it in doing horrible things. There is not really a &quot;oh, this is a dark lens upon you the player&quot; to be held up here unless your players are horrible people, but I'm going to assume most aren't.<br /> Hunters are not monsters. There is nothing about the corebook that really even implies that. Integrity is not Morality and the book goes out of it's way to draw an &quot;us&quot; vs &quot;them&quot; line in several places. Hunters are &quot;he who fights monsters should do well to not become a monster himself&quot;, but they don't start out as monsters. They *potentially* become monsters as a result of the things they experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Making lifesaving medicines that you also price gouge and make through murder is a bad thing. And this problem of &quot;they hunt monsters... and also eat babies!!!&quot; isn't unique to Cheiron.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because those are treated as sympathetic within their own games. Not every vampire is spamming Dominate on everyone they meet and draining everyone to the last health. Not every Promethean is objectifying everyone they meet. I don't actually like or care about Mummy, so I can't really say anything in defense of that one. Those are fine to play as because you're taking extreme stereotypes of how someone could be evil as a member of those templates as opposed to simply letting them exist. Those are also <i>templates</i> you're stereotyping while I'm talking about <i>organizations.</i> You don't really have a choice in if you exist in the world as a Promethean or Vampire, you do have a choice to join an org. But the Ordo Dracul are evil and they're in the game about being a vampire, not the game about being a monster hunter. The Cheiron Group fits within the world of the game, but it doesn't fit the themes of responding to trauma.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> It is just baffling to me that people are essentially arguing that Hunter is somehow uniquely monstrous among the lines and the idea that maybe the overtly antagonistic orgs that are treated <i>in the Hunter book</i> as being exceptionally evil are not really good. Hunters are desperate people who become traumatized. None of the evil Orgs really facilitate that, because despite the arguments to the contrary, they are *not* evil as a result of supernatural trauma. They're evil because they want to make money or fuck monsters and don't even ostensibly care about the victims of themselves or the monsters.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not saying Hunter orgs have to be paragons of justice. I'm just saying that maybe they shouldn't be at the same level as the Vampires who slaughter homeless people just to experiment on them. No one is jonesing to make the Free Council or Spring Court more overtly evil. Why should the Hunter orgs be worse?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ok now. First paragraph response. The Abbey did have that issue. Which they noticed and started refocusing them to be more about &quot;fun&quot; in a broader sense and turning down the sexual crap. Though this did not mean the Abbey DIDNT do it anymore. They do. They own up to it. They know what they do is for the sake of fun, and they aren't gonna pretend that they have some standard to uphold. And do you not realize you literally went into the pitfall they represent? Yes they aren't roleplayers like us. But they ARE doing it for fun. Like us. And dress hiw you want, roleplaying as a hero hunting monsters to save your community. When it comes down to it, it's not the reason you play Hunter. You play it because it's FUN<br /> <br /> Second paragraph. Again, strawmanning cheiron. Yes, the ORGANIZATION is evil. But the people who make up it are victims to monsters just as much as they are to chieron itself. Is invictus pure evil now because the organization encourages treating people like cattle the most? I guess none of its members are sympathetic<br /> <br /> And I don't buy that &quot;actually it's fine to be evil if it's a monster&quot; and ESPECIALLY &quot;they aren't portrayed sympathetically&quot;. Like what? Sympathy for the devil is a huge theme in chronicles of darkness. I'm baffled to hear vampires aren't portrayed as sympathetic that they are forced to feed on people and know forever that most people will only love them in an artificial manner. I always read that they are monsters in terrible circumstances. And you're doing the exact same thing, stereotyping the hunter template while talking about organizations. Also why must the hunter organizations explicitly reflect trauma? That's more of a changeling theme in organizations. The hunter theme of organization is of candles, weak sources of light, coming together to fight off the dark.<br /> <br /> And while it's been in there this whole time, your last paragraph is most explicit, you dont want hunters to be as bad as monsters. You want them to be heroes. Why can't they be as bad as monstrous organizations? Why water down how bad people can be? And using the spring court and free council as examples is whataboutism. They have nothing to do with hunter, and hunter already has groups like that (Yuri, union, 9 stars, etc)<br /> <br /> Yes hunter is a story of be careful when looking into the abyss, but arcane isnt saying they are monsters in the literal sense like vampires. Hes saying they are in the sense that their depravity can be just as bad. The average hunter indeed doesnt start that way. Many get there though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T13:07:30-07:00","id":1514601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514597#post1514597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok now. First paragraph response. The Abbey did have that issue. Which they noticed and started refocusing them to be more about &quot;fun&quot; in a broader sense and turning down the sexual crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually argue the opposite. Tooth and Nail treats the Abbey as being extremely disturbing to the point that even Beasts find them gross and villainous. Meanwhile the 1e corebook has them as hedonists, but doesn't treat them as if they're all rapists. I also don't think &quot;we're doing rapes for fun!&quot; is actually toning things down. The actual context of what is being done is sort of important. &quot;You're just like the Abbey!&quot; isn't true because their fantasy is being rapists and my fantasy is being a traumatized hero.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure you know what the word strawmanning means. I am literally describing their actions as given in the corebook. They price gouge, they harvest monsters that aren't antagonistic, and they even hunt down their own agents if necessary. There is no way to portray them as morally grey because even what good they do is done for unethical reasons and in unethical ways. Comparing the group of monster hunters to the group of secrecy obsessed conspiracy vampires <i>should not favour the vampires</i>, but it does in this case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I don't buy that &quot;actually it's fine to be evil if it's a monster&quot; </div> </div> </div>It's not fine to be evil if you're a monster. It's that being a monster doesn't make you evil. A vampire doesn't need to spam Dominate and eat hobos. A Promethean does not need to play with humans just to find out what makes them tick. A mage does not need to harvest souls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also why must the hunter organizations explicitly reflect trauma? That's more of a changeling theme in organizations. The hunter theme of organization is of candles, weak sources of light, coming together to fight off the dark. </div> </div> </div> The Cheiron Group <i>is not a candle in the dark!!!</i> That's my fucking point here. The most antagonistic and villainous of the Hunter Orgs <i>are not actually within the theme of Hunter the Vigil!</i> The Cheiron Group are not cursed with damnation and required to feed upon the still living blood of the innocent to survive! They aren't evil because they're damned by god, they're evil because it increases their bank account number.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And while it's been in there this whole time, your last paragraph is most explicit, you dont want hunters to be as bad as monsters. You want them to be heroes. Why can't they be as bad as monstrous organizations? Why water down how bad people can be? And using the spring court and free council as examples is whataboutism. They have nothing to do with hunter, and hunter already has groups like that (Yuri, union, 9 stars, etc) </div> </div> </div>The issue here is that Cheiron and Taskforce VALKYRIE are not &quot;as bad as monstrous organizations&quot;, they are actively worse. I don't want to &quot;water down how bad people can be&quot;, I want the game about being monster hunters to not make you actively worse than the fucking monsters. Also, Nine Stars are nothing like Yuri's Group or the Spring Court or Free Council. They're cops. They're crooked cops. No amount of fictionalization will make me ignore the fact that the Hong Kong Police Department are brutally violent and trained in colonialist repression tactics. <br /> <br /> Again: It is baffling to me that people want the monster hunter splat to be filled with evil organizations. Why is it so contentious that I think Hunter Orgs should be more like the Courts or Orders than the Ordo Dracul? Hell, Cheiron is practically on the level of VII or Belial's Brood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T13:15:35-07:00","id":1514605,"title":"","content":"Tired of waiting for it, so:<br /> <br /> Again, I'm at work and just don't have the energy to deconstruct how the emphasis on evil is indicative of not engaging with Hunter's themes, or Chronicles's themes on the whole, for whatever reason, but I do want at least point more in the direction of what my issue is than an admittedly glib response will do, so to that end, I'm gonn post a bit from one scrapped response that I feel still really worked well. <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, Cheiron is not made up of victims. Taskforce VALKYRIE is not made up of victims. </div> </div> </div>You're starting from a top down perspective that is not helping you to understand the picture Hunter is painting.<br /> <br /> The books demonstrate time and again that engagement with the supernatural is not a thing that people casually do for almost any given reason, given that the supernatural in all of it's forms its actively psychologically and spiritually stressful and damaging-most people's responses are to try and keep themselves as distant from the supernatural as they can after one or two exceptional intrustions. Mortal investigators from the Chronicles corebook are often individuals who are in the middle of one of those exceptional intrusions and are written with a general understanding that most of them will go back to not looking too closely at the shadows once a chronicle is over, with a rare few exceptions diving deeper to understand it better to better interact with it (or, more realistically, be even better at not engaging with it, or at least not without protections).<br /> <br /> The sort of person who becomes a hunter, a person who not only interacts and investigates the supernatural but actively work to harm in it a variety of ways in the name of a variety of causes and reasons, is an expectation above and beyond that, and the general root of that is a resolution against the harm they dealt with in their one or two exceptional experiences with the supernatural. Hunter: the Vigil First Edition's corebook is pretty upfront and explicit about that, pretty well opening it's world building chapter at the start of the book with &quot;Yeah, pretty much every hunter is a victim of supernatural violence of some sort.&quot;<br /> <br /> So if you wanted to provide a fuller line, a non-reductive line with this, it might go something like &quot;The Field Projects Division of the Cheiron Group and Task Force: Valkyrie are not, institutionally, victims in any meaningful sense, but there are things about them that are attractive to victims of supernatural violence that lead to making up a lot of those organizations with those victims.&quot;\u200b <hr />And as addendum to that, it's in that attraction that more of the overall point is found.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T14:38:40-07:00","id":1514615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514601#post1514601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually argue the opposite. Tooth and Nail treats the Abbey as being extremely disturbing to the point that even Beasts find them gross and villainous. Meanwhile the 1e corebook has them as hedonists, but doesn't treat them as if they're all rapists. I also don't think &quot;we're doing rapes for fun!&quot; is actually toning things down. The actual context of what is being done is sort of important. &quot;You're just like the Abbey!&quot; isn't true because their fantasy is being rapists and my fantasy is being a traumatized hero.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure you know what the word strawmanning means. I am literally describing their actions as given in the corebook. They price gouge, they harvest monsters that aren't antagonistic, and they even hunt down their own agents if necessary. There is no way to portray them as morally grey because even what good they do is done for unethical reasons and in unethical ways. Comparing the group of monster hunters to the group of secrecy obsessed conspiracy vampires <i>should not favour the vampires</i>, but it does in this case.<br /> <br /> It's not fine to be evil if you're a monster. It's that being a monster doesn't make you evil. A vampire doesn't need to spam Dominate and eat hobos. A Promethean does not need to play with humans just to find out what makes them tick. A mage does not need to harvest souls.<br /> <br /> The Cheiron Group <i>is not a candle in the dark!!!</i> That's my fucking point here. The most antagonistic and villainous of the Hunter Orgs <i>are not actually within the theme of Hunter the Vigil!</i> The Cheiron Group are not cursed with damnation and required to feed upon the still living blood of the innocent to survive! They aren't evil because they're damned by god, they're evil because it increases their bank account number.<br /> <br /> <br /> The issue here is that Cheiron and Taskforce VALKYRIE are not &quot;as bad as monstrous organizations&quot;, they are actively worse. I don't want to &quot;water down how bad people can be&quot;, I want the game about being monster hunters to not make you actively worse than the fucking monsters. Also, Nine Stars are nothing like Yuri's Group or the Spring Court or Free Council. They're cops. They're crooked cops. No amount of fictionalization will make me ignore the fact that the Hong Kong Police Department are brutally violent and trained in colonialist repression tactics.<br /> <br /> Again: It is baffling to me that people want the monster hunter splat to be filled with evil organizations. Why is it so contentious that I think Hunter Orgs should be more like the Courts or Orders than the Ordo Dracul? Hell, Cheiron is practically on the level of VII or Belial's Brood.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they ARE a candle. No one said these candles were the comforting flame. Some come together and are dangerous fires threatening to consume all without mercy. That's what the cheiron group is. They are still on humanities side. And I said nine stars because they are still doing good with what they got. They HAVE to be crooked (and to be honest, yuri's is making things worse).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T14:41:02-07:00","id":1514616,"title":"","content":"And tooth and nail literally makes fun of the Abbey stereotype. Cmon dude","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T15:23:12-07:00","id":1514622,"title":"","content":"I have to say, it's funny to cite the Courts and especially the Orders as &quot;not evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Right, and mages aren't monsters either, I'm sure. [/sarcasm]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T15:53:23-07:00","id":1514628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514622#post1514622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, it's funny to cite the Courts and especially the Orders as &quot;not evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> Right, and mages aren't monsters either, I'm sure. [/sarcasm]</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit. I've been antagonistic to aspel. But I just can't stand these assertions. Spring Court has a nice exterior but they may just leave you to the wolves if it means they get to keep the lamb chops safe for a rowdy feast. And the orders want what's best for MAGES, not humanity as it is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T18:30:06-07:00","id":1514643,"title":"","content":"I have no idea what books you're all reading, but they give very different impressions than the ones I'm reading. There are bad people within the Courts and Orders, but even the worst Orders (the Guardians and Thearchs) are more moral than Cheiron, which is such an evil group that it serves as an example of the antagonists for an entire gameline.<br /> <br /> You can't be a candle in the dark if you <i>are the darkness</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T20:15:22-07:00","id":1514645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514643#post1514643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea what books you're all reading, but they give very different impressions than the ones I'm reading. There are bad people within the Courts and Orders, but even the worst Orders (the Guardians and Thearchs) are more moral than Cheiron, which is such an evil group that it serves as an example of the antagonists for an entire gameline.<br /> <br /> You can't be a candle in the dark if you <i>are the darkness</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I consider the guardians better than the other Orders.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, my opinion of them is better. I don't know how they are better than cheiron. What, the medical group killing monsters, many of which prey on humanity by their very nature, is pure evil for making medicine out of them? But the thearchs, who want to build a society of enlightenment where some are more enlightened than others, is better? The same mages who believe whole heartedly to push magic to the very limit and damn the consequences? Or the mysterium, who houses the most anti sleeper mages that don't condemn killing them to keep Mysteries safe, is better? Or the adamantine arrow, a WAR cult, is good? You know, who believe conflict is not only good, but a wanted state of affairs? Or the Free Council, falling into the same pitfalls of both revolution and democracy, except with magic to back it up?<br /> <br /> The courts are just so good, making deals with innocent people that have no idea what they re getting into are good? Like the summer court poking the hornets next because they just HAVE to fight back even though that invites threat to everyone, humans included? Or the hedonistic spring court, who very well will push anything unsavory under the rug to make things better for themselves even when it's more harm than good? Nevermind what the autumn and winter court do.<br /> <br /> I'm not arguing what's worse, but you're deliberately white washing monstrous organizations while pretending chieron is some great archetypal evil entity. And the thing about that particular playable faction? They're extremely popular. Hunter fans love playing as them. And you can get a great ton of variety with them alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T21:28:08-07:00","id":1514648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514622#post1514622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, it's funny to cite the Courts and especially the Orders as &quot;not evil.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I still vividly remember describing the Seasonal Courts to my mother in pretty plain quick-reference level terms at one point as part of just talking about a game I was interested in and receiving the response of &quot;they sound evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Highlighting this because it's worth emphasizing: while we like to use the name of the conglomerate interchangeably with it, the Field Projects Division is not the same thing as The Cheiron Group as a corporate entity. It is, in fact, repeatedly emphasized within the books as a low-rung branch of the company populated in significant proportion by people desperate and/or greedy enough to hunt monsters with the specific intention of taking them alive or at least harvesting them for parts at the behest of a corporation that demands quotas and may ask them to serve as testbeds for the grody medical prototypes that haven't hit the market yet, because it pays well or it keeps their husband's cancer in remission or it lets them take the fight to the monsters with the backing of a global corporation who can keep the law off their back to a certain degree.<br /> <br /> It is <i>kind of a shit job</i>, as one could probably infer from there being more than one sample character blurb in both corebooks (at least six of the eight) that boils down to &quot;you were put in the Field Projects Division due to a lucrative job offer you didn't properly read, legal trouble you were or could be in that the company would keep at bay, or a clerical error, and now you've got monster parts in you.&quot; The comparison to the Devoted is <i>not a subtle one</i>, particularly with Second Edition putting a little more emphasis on conspiracy hunters going rogue.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bringing it back to changeling courts for a moment: There is a <i>reason</i> I made the more structured side of the Gray City Freehold emotionally resonate with <i>guilt</i>, and it's not because the Fire Court are unvarnished good guys who just feel bad that they can't solve every problem before it happens, even if they do have an institutional mandate to preserve lives. Shared secrets and shared trauma have a way of bringing people together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T22:31:01-07:00","id":1514651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514645#post1514645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. I consider the guardians better than the other Orders.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, my opinion of them is better. I don't know how they are better than cheiron. What, the medical group killing monsters, many of which prey on humanity by their very nature, is pure evil for making medicine out of them? But the thearchs, who want to build a society of enlightenment where some are more enlightened than others, is better? The same mages who believe whole heartedly to push magic to the very limit and damn the consequences? Or the mysterium, who houses the most anti sleeper mages that don't condemn killing them to keep Mysteries safe, is better? Or the adamantine arrow, a WAR cult, is good? You know, who believe conflict is not only good, but a wanted state of affairs? Or the Free Council, falling into the same pitfalls of both revolution and democracy, except with magic to back it up?<br /> <br /> The courts are just so good, making deals with innocent people that have no idea what they re getting into are good? Like the summer court poking the hornets next because they just HAVE to fight back even though that invites threat to everyone, humans included? Or the hedonistic spring court, who very well will push anything unsavory under the rug to make things better for themselves even when it's more harm than good? Nevermind what the autumn and winter court do.<br /> <br /> I'm not arguing what's worse, but you're deliberately white washing monstrous organizations while pretending chieron is some great archetypal evil entity. And the thing about that particular playable faction? They're extremely popular. Hunter fans love playing as them. And you can get a great ton of variety with them alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Argumentum ad populum is also a logical fallacy.<br /> And you're doing quite a lot of whataboutism all throughout.<br /> I'm not even sure what you're arguing <i>for</i> at this point.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T02:13:24-07:00","id":1514671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514645#post1514645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I consider the guardians better than the other Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Guardians are a cult dedicated to murdering people who don't toe the line and ushering in Mage Jesus. They're better than the other Orders only in that what they're facing is an actively hostile malevolent realm that is anathema to reality. One of their core tenants is &quot;sins for a just cause grant wisdom&quot; because they believe done murder for the greater good is Wise. They are extremely hubristic and see themselves as being arbiters of justice and the shepherds of defending reality. Meanwhile you're characterizing Cheiron as if they solely kill evil vampires and brain worms, when that is not how their own write up portrays them. They might kill monsters that prey on humanity. They might put Changelings into the meat grinder to turn them into antidepressants. They're pure evil because they don't give a shit what monsters they chop up, and they don't hand out the results to help people, they price gouge and look for ways to turn a profit as people die from lack of insulin. The thing that you aren't seeming to grasp here when you go &quot;oh, so the war cult is better?&quot; or whatever is that the Adamantine Arrow are not solely violent assholes who get into fights for fun. The Mysterium and Thearchs are not all wizard Nazis. The Summer Court does not &quot;poke the hornets nest&quot; simply because it's fun. The Spring Court is not solely filled with drug dealers and rapists. The Autumn Court and Winter Courts do not all go around and commit serial murder to harvest Fear and Despair.<br /> <br /> That's the point here. Those other factions are <i><b>morally grey</b></i>. They have bad members. Hell, some of their internal goals and conflicts are not good. But they are not solely defined by those aspects. There is not a good Cheiron Field Projects Division agent because <i><b>the things that Cheiron does are all evil</b></i>. They kill not to defend anyone but because of profit. The closest to good an agent could get is not gutting the friendly neighborhood vampire who only feeds on drug dealers until his bosses tell him he has to. And even then the entire structure of the Conspiracy is going to encourage him to see that vampire in terms of dollar signs. Hell, they'll see <i><b>other Hunters</b></i> in terms of dollar signs.<br /> <br /> I'm not white washing anything. The point is not that Courts or Orders or Tribes or whatever else are squeaky clean. The point is that those factions are more nuanced and detailed and capable of aspirational and positive characters than the fucking Hunter Conspiracies I'm complaining about. I don't know how much clearer I can be: <i><b>I do not think that Hunters should be unambiguously good and righteous people, I think that the Organizations should simply not be made up of baby eating evil</b></i>. That Cheiron is a fan favourite means nothing to me. People like the idea of Thaumatechnology. You could have a less evil version of Cheiron and people would still be interested in them. Fans also are aware that Cheiron is evil and it's constantly cited as an example of what Deviant Conspiracies are.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514648#post1514648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still vividly remember describing the Seasonal Courts to my mother in pretty plain quick-reference level terms at one point as part of just talking about a game I was interested in and receiving the response of &quot;they sound evil.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>While feeding off of anger, fear, or sorrow isn't exactly nice, and it's spelled out that desire isn't as nice as it sounds (&quot;I'm starving&quot; is desire), all of the Courts are more than capable of positive characters. Hell, &quot;therapist&quot; is a pretty valid concept for every Court.<br /> Being the low rung or not, Field Projects Division actively commits evil in service of capital. They do what they're told, and the things they're told are bad. &quot;You were actually forced to do this on pain of death&quot; being the most common way to have a moral character in the org is a bad sign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T05:24:39-07:00","id":1514683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514671#post1514671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Guardians are a cult dedicated to murdering people who don't toe the line and ushering in Mage Jesus. They're better than the other Orders only in that what they're facing is an actively hostile malevolent realm that is anathema to reality. One of their core tenants is &quot;sins for a just cause grant wisdom&quot; because they believe done murder for the greater good is Wise. They are extremely hubristic and see themselves as being arbiters of justice and the shepherds of defending reality. Meanwhile you're characterizing Cheiron as if they solely kill evil vampires and brain worms, when that is not how their own write up portrays them. They might kill monsters that prey on humanity. They might put Changelings into the meat grinder to turn them into antidepressants. They're pure evil because they don't give a shit what monsters they chop up, and they don't hand out the results to help people, they price gouge and look for ways to turn a profit as people die from lack of insulin. The thing that you aren't seeming to grasp here when you go &quot;oh, so the war cult is better?&quot; or whatever is that the Adamantine Arrow are not solely violent assholes who get into fights for fun. The Mysterium and Thearchs are not all wizard Nazis. The Summer Court does not &quot;poke the hornets nest&quot; simply because it's fun. The Spring Court is not solely filled with drug dealers and rapists. The Autumn Court and Winter Courts do not all go around and commit serial murder to harvest Fear and Despair.<br /> <br /> That's the point here. Those other factions are <i><b>morally grey</b></i>. They have bad members. Hell, some of their internal goals and conflicts are not good. But they are not solely defined by those aspects. There is not a good Cheiron Field Projects Division agent because <i><b>the things that Cheiron does are all evil</b></i>. They kill not to defend anyone but because of profit. The closest to good an agent could get is not gutting the friendly neighborhood vampire who only feeds on drug dealers until his bosses tell him he has to. And even then the entire structure of the Conspiracy is going to encourage him to see that vampire in terms of dollar signs. Hell, they'll see <i><b>other Hunters</b></i> in terms of dollar signs.<br /> <br /> I'm not white washing anything. The point is not that Courts or Orders or Tribes or whatever else are squeaky clean. The point is that those factions are more nuanced and detailed and capable of aspirational and positive characters than the fucking Hunter Conspiracies I'm complaining about. I don't know how much clearer I can be: <i><b>I do not think that Hunters should be unambiguously good and righteous people, I think that the Organizations should simply not be made up of baby eating evil</b></i>. That Cheiron is a fan favourite means nothing to me. People like the idea of Thaumatechnology. You could have a less evil version of Cheiron and people would still be interested in them. Fans also are aware that Cheiron is evil and it's constantly cited as an example of what Deviant Conspiracies are.<br /> \u200b<br /> While feeding off of anger, fear, or sorrow isn't exactly nice, and it's spelled out that desire isn't as nice as it sounds (&quot;I'm starving&quot; is desire), all of the Courts are more than capable of positive characters. Hell, &quot;therapist&quot; is a pretty valid concept for every Court.<br /> Being the low rung or not, Field Projects Division actively commits evil in service of capital. They do what they're told, and the things they're told are bad. &quot;You were actually forced to do this on pain of death&quot; being the most common way to have a moral character in the org is a bad sign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thr guardians are the one Order who acknowledge mages need to be kept in check, both for their own good and for the good of sleepers. They try to find those worthy of awakening and fool the ones who would inflict harm with it. They have the esoteric tenants part due to symbolic resonance and is rooted in the idea it will save the world WHILE holding them accountable for their actions. They consider just having magic a moral responsibility. I don't know how on earth they are any more hubristic than the other Orders, especially since the ladder is the one stereotyped as saying there is no such thing as hubris<br /> <br /> youre the one pretending the cheiron group is exclusively targeting the nice guy vampire only eating rats (as if that would last) and poor changeling just trying to get his life together. I never acted like they only target the most evil of the evil (which no hunter does. They hunt any they consider a threat or fit their agenda). And why are you pretending they are just selling medicine? Are you going to ignore all the implications there is more to them than just a pharmaceutical company? They have big plans, not just for making money but for humanity and its relationship to monsters in general. You're acting like they're Pentex at this point. Also, you're making that up to say that the end goal is price gouging dude. Finally, they are morally grey. Yes, it kills monsters and doesn't care how evil the monster is (ignoring many prey on humanity by nature. A man eating crocodile isn't evil. You still kill it), yes they do make medicine to sell for profit. They are also killing monsters that prey on people, and making life saving medicine and advancements. And they do have a secret goal that may or may not be good in the end. And why make the group less evil? Fans like both the abilities they grant and the black comedy and tone the organization presents along with its story hooks<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11959\" data-vbnamecard=\"11959\">Niknokk</a> it's not whataboutism to compare the evil of other organizations when the op is arguing that one deserves to be unplayable due to being &quot;evil&quot;. And it's not a fallacy to say that maybe the playable faction shouldnt be made unplayable when it's very popular with the player base. Like, not a good idea at all<br /> <br /> To clarify, I said whataboutism earlier because the free council and spring court were being used as examples of &quot;good&quot; organizations as if that meant that hunter orgs should be &quot;good&quot; organizations. Other than ignoring that those orgs just have a nice coat of paint. As for your accusation, I'm stating that it makes little sense to say you can't have evil organizations in hunter as playable when the other gamelines let you play as explicitly evil organizations despite maintaining a &quot;grey&quot; morality (Invictus, demon Agendas, the Devoted, mummy cults). Now note, these organizations still have moral complexity. But when you look at them as a whole, any normal person would say they are evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 06-12-2023, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T10:56:15-07:00","id":1514720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514683#post1514683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The guardians are the one Order who acknowledge mages need to be kept in check, both for their own good and for the good of sleepers. They try to find those worthy of awakening and fool the ones who would inflict harm with it. They have the esoteric tenants part due to symbolic resonance and is rooted in the idea it will save the world WHILE holding them accountable for their actions. They consider just having magic a moral responsibility. I don't know how on earth they are any more hubristic than the other Orders, especially since the ladder is the one stereotyped as saying there is no such thing as hubris</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I must keep power from the unworthy [because I am the most worthy]&quot; is the definition of hubris. Hubris is to believe you are greater than the Gods. To believe you get to decide destiny.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And why are you pretending they are just selling medicine? Are you going to ignore all the implications there is more to them than just a pharmaceutical company? They have big plans, not just for making money but for humanity and its relationship to monsters in general. </div> </div> </div>Considering they're run by alien starfish, &quot;they have big plans&quot; is not something that makes them less villainous. I don't care if Cheiron *only* kills the nice monsters, that's not the point. The point is that they don't give a shit which monsters they kill, meaning they <i><b>are absolutely going to kill the nice monsters</b></i>, as opposed to groups like The Lucifuge who will basically live and let live. Killing a man eating crocodile so you can turn it's hide into a purse doesn't make you morally grey just because the crocodile eats people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk\">Niknokk</a> it's not whataboutism to compare the evil of other organizations when the op is arguing that one deserves to be unplayable due to being &quot;evil&quot;. And it's not a fallacy to say that maybe the playable faction shouldnt be made unplayable when it's very popular with the player base. Like, not a good idea at all </div> </div> </div>Seers are playable. Loyalists are playable. Belial's Brood are playable. Pure are playable. I never said they shouldn't be playable. I said they shouldn't be presented in the player section and should instead be antagonist factions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now note, these organizations still have moral complexity. But when you look at them as a whole, any normal person would say they are evil. </div> </div> </div> No, most people would not actually say the Courts or Orders are evil. Because they're protagonist factions and the players are supposed to associate with them and find them in some way aspirational. The &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot; is not actually a game about being morally repugnant monsters, it's still a game about playing heroic characters, even if their heroism is closer to Frank Castle than Peter Parker.<br /> And the issue is that Cheiron does not have moral complexity. Taskforce VALKYRIE does not actually have much moral complexity either. &quot;Well they're basically serial killers but sometimes they make insulin or give changelings fake IDs&quot; is not moral complexity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T13:06:14-07:00","id":1514743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514720#post1514720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I must keep power from the unworthy [because I am the most worthy]&quot; is the definition of hubris. Hubris is to believe you are greater than the Gods. To believe you get to decide destiny.<br /> Considering they're run by alien starfish, &quot;they have big plans&quot; is not something that makes them less villainous. I don't care if Cheiron *only* kills the nice monsters, that's not the point. The point is that they don't give a shit which monsters they kill, meaning they <i><b>are absolutely going to kill the nice monsters</b></i>, as opposed to groups like The Lucifuge who will basically live and let live. Killing a man eating crocodile so you can turn it's hide into a purse doesn't make you morally grey just because the crocodile eats people.<br /> <br /> Seers are playable. Loyalists are playable. Belial's Brood are playable. Pure are playable. I never said they shouldn't be playable. I said they shouldn't be presented in the player section and should instead be antagonist factions.<br /> <br /> No, most people would not actually say the Courts or Orders are evil. Because they're protagonist factions and the players are supposed to associate with them and find them in some way aspirational. The &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot; is not actually a game about being morally repugnant monsters, it's still a game about playing heroic characters, even if their heroism is closer to Frank Castle than Peter Parker.<br /> And the issue is that Cheiron does not have moral complexity. Taskforce VALKYRIE does not actually have much moral complexity either. &quot;Well they're basically serial killers but sometimes they make insulin or give changelings fake IDs&quot; is not moral complexity.</div> </div> </div> </div>first paragraph: uhh, that is such a biased and misunderstood perspective of the guardians. Like holy shit. The Guardians don't consider themselves more worthy. They are pragmatic enough to realize that some people SHOULDNT have the power of Awakened people. Moreover, &quot;paradox strengthens the abyss, punishment answers pride&quot; and &quot;merit must guide the fallen world&quot; mean that the exoteric tenants alone mean that they consider the failure to contain paradox as a moral failing (none of the others, especially the ladder and somewhat the ladder, consider paradox this), and means that guardians are the mages most likely to try and follow merit based recognition. As for the esoteric tenants, &quot;all thrones are false, all souls are flawed&quot; and &quot;the heiromagus will fulfill the diamond wheel&quot;. The first applies to guardians too. The second adds not only will the heiromagus NOT come from the guardians, but that the guardians are NOT worthy and will be judged for what they have done. As for &quot;sins for a just end grant wisdom&quot; if you read after that, it's not saying they can commit evil and be rewarded for it. At all. It means they can pass hubris into themselves rather than the other Orders, and purify the diamond wheel. Oh and the hubris you described is something all mages share. <br /> <br /> Second paragraph: so being &quot;starfish aliens&quot; means they are pure evil while vampires and spirits and demons aren't. Got it. Second, there is no &quot;nice monster&quot;. The best a monster can do is minimize the harm they do to humanity. Letting one go is an acknowledgement it will continue to harm people and may get even worse.<br /> <br /> Third paragraph: belials Brood, loyalists, etc are &quot;playable&quot; in only the sense they share the same template. Otherwise they do not share all the story hooks and narrative support that the compacts and conspiracies do. They also do not share the same themes as the playable monsters. ALL the compacts and conspiracies share the themes around being hunters. That is undeniable. Also seers are shown in the playable section, because while they aren't necessarily meant to be played, they still share with their counterparts the theme of being mages. I have no idea why you think they must be antagonist when they bring in more as a playable focus.<br /> <br /> Last paragraph: from a human perspective, yes, people would consider most if not all those factions evil. Also most players play chronicles as sympathetic monsters. Not just the punisher. And again there you go pretending that cheiron and Valkrie only do one good thing. Stop strawmanning dude","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T14:32:02-07:00","id":1514761,"title":"","content":"To quote Awakening 2nd Editions developer,<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1104161-why-do-you-think-beast-is-good-bad/page4#post1105251\"> the Awakened are, barring a few saintly and Wise exceptions, Right Shits</a>. There's a whole chapter in the book about how even the Pentacle are right shits (the Sleepers and Sleepwalkers Appendix).<br /> <br /> The only remainder of the commentary is that there are no baby eating evil hunter organizations (Well, maybe the Hunt Club, and the failure to mention them Has Been Noted For Gameline Literacy), and while I'll freely admit that it doesn't help trying to engage this thread while I don't have the time to do so properly*, the escalation to this extreme and failure to deviate away from it leaves me wondering leaves me wondering if we have a point in actually doing that.<br /> <br /> Like, yes, Hunter is a game of being a light in shadows, but it's also very much asking what that means, and the game does take a stance that some answers to that question are invalid. If you cannot comprehend the darkness, you cannot meaningfully be a light in it. Failing to engage with that darkness beyond an idea of evil is basically a fast track to Hunter's darkest depths as monsters, and that includes the organizations that emerge from basic hunter psychology.<br /> <br /> Hunters <i>aren't the good guys</i>, and because of that, <i>the organizations they form cannot be the good guys, <u>but there is a whole world of nuance and thought on morality and ethics beyond that once you accept that Hunters are not the good guys.</u></i> I don't really know what to say to anyone not wanting to engage with and understand the humanity present in pretty much any hunter that is the root cause for the creation and growth of those evil organizations, beyond &quot;That sort of thing is textually called out with slashers&quot; and &quot;Why are you playing any Chronicles game at all?&quot;***<br /> <br /> *though, in mild defense here, a proper engagement means having to actually explain from the ground up, including but not limited to explaining the narrative and thematic way Chronicles approaches &quot;evil&quot; and monstrosity and to the end of understanding and allowing for a complexity of humanity as understanding, the fact that hunters being grouped as the same vampires, werewolves, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/933516-why-not-witches/page2#post933962\">witches</a>, constructs, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen?p=820117#post820117\">fairies</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew#post1343937\">ghosts</a>, mummies, demons, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1394516-the-humanity-of-beast-the-primordial#post1394516\">mythic monsters</a>, and abberations is a meaningful and deliberate point, the way organizational principles and structures work in Chronicles of Darkness regarding those themes and how utterly divorced all of that is from simple black and white morality and instead with the themes and circumstances the games are talking about, the way Hunter takes every other gameline to task by nakedly going after the effects of their actions while stripping away the justifications offered by the circumstances, but then turns right around and does that to itself** as well, and laying out how the actionability of all that brings us right back around to honoring the humanity that drives people to monstrosity while still leaving room to combat that monstrostiy, and doing all of that in enough detail that it's not only clear enough for people who never read the books but is substantial enough that dissenting opinions dervied from it correspondingly have enough substance to actually be a worthwhile alternative opinion and not uninformed noise, and given all of that alongside the rest of my life, I hope I can be forgiven for not quite having had the time to do that yet.<br /> **in contrast to Beast which strips justifications away from all other splats and shows them who they are to themselves-Hunter handling consequences of actions and Beast handling the consequences of being solidly covering internal and external consequences which honestly does a lot to make it clear what is that actual moral and ethical concerns of Chronicles on the whole.<br /> ***I mean, I suppose we could also discuss the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822143-ever-getting-a-hero?p=822618#post822618\">Princess Problem</a> or the matter of expectations for tropes and archetypes for a game about monster hunters, but given that the conversation is hung up on a theme of &quot;those who hunt monsters&quot; that is is setup with the cover and built upon from there with reading, I'm not sure getting into particularly deeper reads resolves the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T22:51:41-07:00","id":1514801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514761#post1514761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822143-ever-getting-a-hero?p=822618#post822618\">Princess Problem</a>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that.<br /> <br /> &quot;How Princess the Hopeful doesnt fit in the COFD. How it lacks Mystery, how it lacks uncertainty&quot;<br /> <br /> Now I ask of you did we read the same book or have you gone RAPT<br /> <br /> The Uncertainty in PtH is wondering if your changes on the world will STICK,and while you are GOOD , unquestionable,you are in a horrible world, where you have to fight tooth and nail to make a change, and it's EXHAUSTING<br /> <br /> And there will be people who will undo all your hard work, given the chance, and that's the Mystery, who to trust, Who is going to stick to their ideals, in a place where most people throw away their for short term gain.<br /> <br /> Included in that post you made you brushed off the Twilight Courts, which have been around longer and are more Organized, while also giving princess easy answers to complex problems.<br /> THEY ARE SOMETHING TO TAKE SERIOUSLY<br /> <br /> <br /> FOR FUCKS SAKE THEIR IS A CITY STATE(or a dozen, depending on your storyteller picks on the courts) OF TWILIGHTS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27385,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","user":"Cross-a-way","date":". 06-13-2023, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T07:54:21-07:00","id":1514844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514761#post1514761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scr