and doing all of that in enough detail that it's not only clear enough for people who never read the books but is substantial enough that dissenting opinions dervied from it correspondingly have enough substance to actually be a worthwhile alternative opinion and not uninformed noise, and given all of that alongside the rest of my life, I hope I can be forgiven for not quite having had the time to do that yet.<br /> **in contrast to Beast which strips justifications away from all other splats and shows them who they are to themselves-Hunter handling consequences of actions and Beast handling the consequences of being solidly covering internal and external consequences which honestly does a lot to make it clear what is that actual moral and ethical concerns of Chronicles on the whole.<br /> ***I mean, I suppose we could also discuss the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822143-ever-getting-a-hero?p=822618#post822618\">Princess Problem</a> or the matter of expectations for tropes and archetypes for a game about monster hunters, but given that the conversation is hung up on a theme of &quot;those who hunt monsters&quot; that is is setup with the cover and built upon from there with reading, I'm not sure getting into particularly deeper reads resolves the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hunt club was mentioned actually. But aspel also said the Melbourne rules were alright. So...yeah. take what you will for what is considered a good faction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T12:18:11-07:00","id":1514869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514743#post1514743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guardians don't consider themselves more worthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I am the one capable of making the decisions here&quot; is an implicit statement of worthiness. Also stop calling me dude. Maybe I should take a cue from Arc and put that in my bio.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514761#post1514761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters <i>aren't the good guys</i>, and because of that, the organizations they form cannot be the good guys</div> </div> </div> </div>Your argument is circular. &quot;Hunters aren't the good guys, just look at the organizations Hunters form.&quot; The problem is that there are good Hunter organizations. If you want to focus on the negatives at the elimination of everything else and all your Spring Courtiers are sexual abusers and all your Mystagogues are wizard racists, and all your Hunters are one step from turning into a serial killer if they see you using a grimoire, then fine, whatever. But that isn't actually what the actual books show. That isn't actually what the mechanics of the game imply. And frankly I don't think that's how most people actually play the game, because most of the time when players <i>are</i> doing bad things, they and even their Storytellers don't actually think about whether their actions would effect the NPCs because the NPCs aren't real people and have about as much agency as Fargoth looking for his missing ring.<br /> <br /> Even the people who do play Cheiron agents and members of the Abbey probably aren't thinking about how horrible the things they're doing are. And I doubt that STs are running it so that every Cheiron agent is going after the vegetarian vampires who play Spider-Man to a neighborhood, because the only decisions there are &quot;kill the noble monster&quot; and &quot;get killed by your boss&quot; and that plotline doesn't really stay interesting after doing it so often.<br /> <br /> I just don't see the arguments either of you are making as holding water. I don't think &quot;actually all these organizations are just as evil anyway&quot; is true, since half the stories I see of people's characters and all the people I've ever played with tend to play noble and idealistic characters. Even when they play Guardians or Arrows people aren't playing some serial killer trying to bring about the Heiromagus' reign through blood, but that's a pretty explicit potential character. And Hunters may not necessarily be paragons of virtue considering they interact with the world through violence, but even in the given organizations there are plenty that do otherwise. You are the one getting hung up on &quot;he who fights monsters&quot;, not me. Because to me a character who is threatened with Integrity damage and on the road to slasherdom is not actually the kind of player character people actually play unless they're explicitly trying to do that and make it happen. People are not playing Rufus because Rufus is actually a boring character, they're playing Sam and Dean because Sam and Dean are interesting characters. Or at least attractive characters. And Supernatural is deep into Spooky Cops\u2122 territory where all monsters are actually evil and bad and any time they said otherwise was just a trick. So Rufus is not only morally justified in extreme prejudice, he's tactically correct. And yet even in that world where there <i><b>are</b></i> no good monsters, and every one of them that tries to keep in check is just naive, wanton vampire serial murder is treated as bad.<br /> Which is exactly the tone that Hunter the Vigil goes for.<br /> <br /> In fact, frankly the book takes an even more idealistic view of Hunters than I do in places. Up until it talks about boner pills and black sites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T13:14:47-07:00","id":1514874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514869#post1514869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I am the one capable of making the decisions here&quot; is an implicit statement of worthiness. Also stop calling me dude. Maybe I should take a cue from Arc and put that in my bio.<br /> <br /> Your argument is circular. &quot;Hunters aren't the good guys, just look at the organizations Hunters form.&quot; The problem is that there are good Hunter organizations. If you want to focus on the negatives at the elimination of everything else and all your Spring Courtiers are sexual abusers and all your Mystagogues are wizard racists, and all your Hunters are one step from turning into a serial killer if they see you using a grimoire, then fine, whatever. But that isn't actually what the actual books show. That isn't actually what the mechanics of the game imply. And frankly I don't think that's how most people actually play the game, because most of the time when players <i>are</i> doing bad things, they and even their Storytellers don't actually think about whether their actions would effect the NPCs because the NPCs aren't real people and have about as much agency as Fargoth looking for his missing ring.<br /> <br /> Even the people who do play Cheiron agents and members of the Abbey probably aren't thinking about how horrible the things they're doing are. And I doubt that STs are running it so that every Cheiron agent is going after the vegetarian vampires who play Spider-Man to a neighborhood, because the only decisions there are &quot;kill the noble monster&quot; and &quot;get killed by your boss&quot; and that plotline doesn't really stay interesting after doing it so often.<br /> <br /> I just don't see the arguments either of you are making as holding water. I don't think &quot;actually all these organizations are just as evil anyway&quot; is true, since half the stories I see of people's characters and all the people I've ever played with tend to play noble and idealistic characters. Even when they play Guardians or Arrows people aren't playing some serial killer trying to bring about the Heiromagus' reign through blood, but that's a pretty explicit potential character. And Hunters may not necessarily be paragons of virtue considering they interact with the world through violence, but even in the given organizations there are plenty that do otherwise. You are the one getting hung up on &quot;he who fights monsters&quot;, not me. Because to me a character who is threatened with Integrity damage and on the road to slasherdom is not actually the kind of player character people actually play unless they're explicitly trying to do that and make it happen. People are not playing Rufus because Rufus is actually a boring character, they're playing Sam and Dean because Sam and Dean are interesting characters. Or at least attractive characters. And Supernatural is deep into Spooky Cops\u2122 territory where all monsters are actually evil and bad and any time they said otherwise was just a trick. So Rufus is not only morally justified in extreme prejudice, he's tactically correct. And yet even in that world where there <i><b>are</b></i> no good monsters, and every one of them that tries to keep in check is just naive, wanton vampire serial murder is treated as bad.<br /> Which is exactly the tone that Hunter the Vigil goes for.<br /> <br /> In fact, frankly the book takes an even more idealistic view of Hunters than I do in places. Up until it talks about boner pills and black sites.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize for calling you that.<br /> <br /> yeah, the guardians consider themselves worthy enough to make these judgements. They also judge themselves and each other to make sure they haven't gone corrupt. And ALL mages believe themselves more worthy then sleepers, even the free council","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T15:17:12-07:00","id":1514884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514801#post1514801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh that.<br /> <br /> &quot;How Princess the Hopeful doesnt fit in the COFD. How it lacks Mystery, how it lacks uncertainty&quot;<br /> <br /> Now I ask of you did we read the same book or have you gone RAPT<br /> <br /> The Uncertainty in PtH is wondering if your changes on the world will STICK,and while you are GOOD , unquestionable,you are in a horrible world, where you have to fight tooth and nail to make a change, and it's EXHAUSTING<br /> <br /> And there will be people who will undo all your hard work, given the chance, and that's the Mystery, who to trust, Who is going to stick to their ideals, in a place where most people throw away their for short term gain.<br /> <br /> Included in that post you made you brushed off the Twilight Courts, which have been around longer and are more Organized, while also giving princess easy answers to complex problems.<br /> THEY ARE SOMETHING TO TAKE SERIOUSLY<br /> <br /> <br /> FOR FUCKS SAKE THEIR IS A CITY STATE(or a dozen, depending on your storyteller picks on the courts) OF TWILIGHTS.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I have never read the fangame that I very frequently point out as my favorite and use a model that points the way for how fangames can be their best. You have soundly defeated me, and I must now go reside in a cave to recover from the shame inflicted upon me.<br /> <br /> Or I could just borrow a quote <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822143-ever-getting-a-hero?p=823059#post823059\">from Satchel </a>that handily addresses this misconception.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822143-ever-getting-a-hero?p=823059#post823059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've demonstrated on multiple occasions that you are a practical virtuoso at the art of not paying attention, but fuck it, let's unpack this.<br /> <br /> You were told that Princess doesn't work on the basis that mystery and uncertainty are the core themes of the Chronicles of Darkness and knowing that you're unambiguously &quot;the good guys&quot; is at odds with this.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> The Light that Princess deals with is unambiguously good and the Darkness that it deals with is unambiguously bad to such a degree that its associated antagonist-types are sellouts, lunatics, animals, and Actual Witches From Madoka Magica. There's no meaningful nuance in the interaction between sides save for how resource-poaching from or by the Twilight Queens tweaks the numbers one way or the other.<br /> <br /> That doesn't make for a metaphysic that meshes well with a setting whose magic is mysterious as a rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for the actual current direction of the conversation, Yep, that sure could have been summarized with &quot;You are correct, I am not going to engage with the humanistic themes of Chronicles or the actual text of Hunter, good day ma'am.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, I do have one more clarification before checking out, I very clearly wasn't saying &quot;Hunters aren't good guys because of the organizations they make&quot; I was saying &quot;the morality that comes with what it takes to be a hunter is explicitly compromised from the get go on multiple fronts, to such that there is no way to be an inarguable good guy, and as such any organization that is built by and made up of hunters will carry that same collective moral compromise.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm pretty big on Chronicles as a setting where people is peoples. I run games where vampires lose their mind because they've lost the Prince's dog, where Changelings are dealing with the stress of setting up a festival, where hunters act as diplomats to de-escalate tensions between monstrous factions. I'm an open advocate for heroic characters in all venues. There's a lot of bright, human, and optimistic ways to explore Chronicles' themes and ideas.<br /> <br /> But if you don't own the monstrosity of every splat as it stands, and you don't respect the humanism that's being explored with that monstrosity, then you're not reading or playing Chronicles, you're reading/playing a fanfic headcanon version of it, and quite frankly that's makes your criticisms useless for anyone interested in Chronicles.<br /> <br /> If you want to take down the fence, you first need to demonstrate an understanding of why the fence was put up in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-13-2023, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T15:22:55-07:00","id":1514885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514874#post1514874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, the guardians consider themselves worthy enough to make these judgements. They also judge themselves and each other to make sure they haven't gone corrupt.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Quis custodiet ipsos custodes</i>\u200b?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514884#post1514884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the actual current direction of the conversation, Yep, that sure could have been summarized with &quot;You are correct, I am not going to engage with the humanistic themes of Chronicles or the actual text of Hunter, good day ma'am.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see how your view of Hunter as definitively &quot;not good guys&quot; is engaging with humanistic themes. Also if you can have arguments about what your favourite gameline's themes actually are, as well as what the themes of Hunter actually are, maybe that's a sign that these things are not so clear to others as they are to you, and that your approach to them is not the approach that everyone has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T16:37:51-07:00","id":1514895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514885#post1514885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Quis custodiet ipsos custodes</i>\u200b?<br /> <br /> I don't really see how your view of Hunter as definitively &quot;not good guys&quot; is engaging with humanistic themes. Also if you can have arguments about what your favourite gameline's themes actually are, as well as what the themes of Hunter actually are, maybe that's a sign that these things are not so clear to others as they are to you, and that your approach to them is not the approach that everyone has.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoting a platitude in Latin or whatever that is doesn't change the fact the guardians not only watch each other, but as part of THEIR VERY SYMBOLISM, are hated by the other Orders who will always doubt them and keep an eye on them where they can","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T17:29:52-07:00","id":1514900,"title":"","content":"I believe that was &quot;who watches the watchmen&quot;. Which... it's the <i>Guardians,</i> that's literally a core component of their whole shtick. They are both the watched and the watchmen. The Orders are meant to be <i>deeply</i> grey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 06-13-2023, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T18:00:38-07:00","id":1514902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514900#post1514900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that was &quot;who watches the watchmen&quot;. Which... it's the <i>Guardians,</i> that's literally a core component of their whole shtick. They are both the watchers and the watchmen. The Orders are meant to be <i>deeply</i> grey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I know what it meant. I just don't think it does anything to make them seem worse than the inherent orders","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T18:34:02-07:00","id":1514904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514902#post1514902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I know what it meant. I just don't think it does anything to make them seem worse than the inherent orders</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, certainly not. Anyone who plays the Orders as solely Good or soley Evil is entirely missing the point of Mage. The Pentacle are <i>protagonists</i>, the question is just what lines they consider crossable. A protagonist is not necessarily a good guy.<br /> <br /> If I have to hazard a guess based on this thread and that one link earlier, Aspel seems to take issue with Authority. I'm probably not articulating this well, but... structure, &quot;big government&quot;, law enforcement, military, etc. Which... fair, Authority gets twisted into Authoritatian and Fascist pretty easily. But like anything else, you can't just throw the baby out with the bathwater because it doesn't perfectly align with your vision of the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit -<br /> <br /> Also, <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514720#post1514720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seers are playable. Loyalists are playable. Belial's Brood are playable. Pure are playable. I never said they shouldn't be playable. I said they shouldn't be presented in the player section and should instead be antagonist factions.</div> </div> </div> </div> Is objectively wrong. Possibly splitting hairs, but Seers are presented throughout 2e's core as a viable play option. You'll need to plan accordingly, but all their options are <i>right there</i> alongside the Pentacle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 06-13-2023, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T18:37:23-07:00","id":1514905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514869#post1514869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I doubt that STs are running it so that every Cheiron agent is going after the vegetarian vampires who play Spider-Man to a neighborhood, because the only decisions there are &quot;kill the noble monster&quot; and &quot;get killed by your boss&quot; and that plotline doesn't really stay interesting after doing it so often.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the second time you've brought up the Friendly Neighborhood Vampire thing as one of the only possible routes for an FPD agent to do good in the world, so I feel it is worth pointing out what kind of monsters tend to attract hunters' attention in general and also present a reminder of basic predatory practices. Which is to say:<br /> <br /> 1. If you're a monster and hunters are after you, you fucked up. Maybe you broke an oath or never swore one to begin with. Maybe you're the only thing like you in town and still figuring out your limits and the way secrecy works. Maybe you put your trust in the wrong person/ritual/other monster. Very possibly you are an animal or an automaton or an extremely disoriented Thing From Beyond The World. Whatever the case, if hunters are after you it's because something you did or failed to do led to you being found out and determined to be in need of hunting.<br /> <br /> 2. If you're a hunter conspiracy looking for monsters in a proactive fashion (e.g. to collect them for parts or as guinea pigs), you go for the easy targets first, and you use the minimum of resources needed to take them down or take them in where possible. That means not going after targets with a functioning support network if you can't get them out of it. That means finding targets that people will be glad to be rid of. That means avoiding a fight if a fight can be avoided, whether through diplomacy or subterfuge or blackmail or overwhelming force multiplier advantage. There's if you just need a vampire, no need to go after the Spiderman wannabe if his sire left half a dozen revenants stumbling around the East Side who you won't have to engineer a smear campaign for, just like you needn't go for his sire (provided you know about him) unless those revenants are acting as an unliving smokescreen for the fact that the old bloodsucker's sleeping the sleep of the ages for a couple of years after one wild night.<br /> <br /> Cheiron expects its agents to meet quotas. The easiest way to meet those quotas is to keep an eye out for monsters making themselves obvious enough to be the subject of a story in a Hunter game. The easiest way to make yourself obvious enough to be the subject of a Hunter game, as a monster, is to do something stupid or careless or unlucky, which most characters enmeshed in the societies of monsters other gamelines have as focal points are smart enough or connected enough to avoid doing for various reasons, most of them to do with secrecy and concern for the well-being of themselves and/or people whose well-being they are invested in. Sometimes they do these things because they got cocky or bet on the wrong horse or didn't have the intelligence or wherewithal to avoid a security camera or an eyewitness.<br /> <br /> Cheiron does not specially exempt its agents from going after monsters who are not personlike actors, and the fact that most of the uses they intend to put those monsters toward don't care whether they're people means the FPD's core strain is &quot;your day job is finding and capturing a certain number of supernaturally-empowered monsters in a certain amount of time, consequences to life and limb and mental health be damned,&quot; with &quot;some of those monsters have human or humanlike intelligence&quot; as much of an adjustable dial as it is for every other hunter who spends any length of time hunting more than one kind of monster. You can run a Cheiron game where a Field Projects Division team is hunkered down in a small town with a cryptid infestation and the main drama comes from not being able to talk with their family about the work they do or what happened at work that gave them third-degree burns long before they have to cope with the trauma of bagging and tagging a clique of teenagers with psychic brainworms.<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is that it is <i>very</i> hard to take &quot;It's impossible to play a hunter working for the Cheiron Group who isn't baby-eating evil&quot; as a good-faith argument that happens to be hyperbolically stated when it leans so hard into the assumption that Hunter's big baked-in wrinkle to playing the archetypal derivations of witch-hunters and Van Helsing is disproportionately front-and-center compared to <i>the kinds of monsters who are the antagonists in a monster-hunting game.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T19:41:11-07:00","id":1514909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514904#post1514904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is objectively wrong. Possibly splitting hairs, but Seers are presented throughout 2e's core as a viable play option. You'll need to plan accordingly, but all their options are <i>right there</i> alongside the Pentacle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that even though they're put right there in the Orders section, it's made clear that they're antagonists. The entire Seers of the Throne are given one write up instead of being split into different factions, and the write up makes it pretty clear that they're the bad guys. It's about presentation. You also can't exactly play a mixed Order game with a Seer unless something is *very* off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514902#post1514902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I know what it meant. I just don't think it does anything to make them seem worse than the inherent orders</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that the Guardians police themselves. They clearly cannot be trusted to do so when their entire focus is about how they are the ones who are allowed to make the decision. &quot;I have audited myself for poor behavior and found that I was correct, case closed&quot;. Does that sound reasonable to you?<br /> It's also not really about making them &quot;seem worse&quot;, it's about pointing out how silly &quot;they're the best&quot; sounds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514905#post1514905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the second time you've brought up the Friendly Neighborhood Vampire thing as one of the only possible routes for an FPD agent to do good in the world</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, my argument is that killing the Friendly Neighborhood Vampire is how a Cheiron Field Projects Division agent is likely to <b><i>do evil</i></b> in the world. Yes, most of the time even Cheiron will be going after the villainous monsters, because those are the ones most easily spotted. But they're also likely to go after the safer option, which means the nice guy vampire who doesn't have a thousand kills and only feeds on drug dealers. Cheiron in particular is likely going to be on the lookout for those kind of easy to bag monsters. They aren't looking for the thrill of the hunt, they don't want to go after Alucard, they want to go after the Potency 1 Horror that lives in the sewer and scares gangbangers away from giving drugs to kids.<br /> The reason it's impossible to play a Hunter working for the Cheiron Group that isn't a baby eating monster is because the Cheiron Group is a group of baby eating monsters. Just because they don't send you, personally, to always go after the baby monsters doesn't mean it isn't on the list of things they want you to do. Hell, I've actually got the outline of a story for a Dragonslayer Knight (Order of Saint George) who falls for a wizard and realizes that he can't put it off anymore and her number is up, and how he reacts to that.<br /> <br /> No, every antagonist will not be the nice vegetarian vampire or woobie changelings. Again, that isn't the point. The point is that <i><b>as a faction</b></i> they don't give a shit. That is baked into their write ups. Meanwhile there are plenty of factions who realize that vampires and witches and faeries and ghostwalkers <i><b>are all still rational, thinking beings</b></i>. So the competing notion of &quot;every Hunter org has to be evil because that's the game you're playing&quot; also doesn't sit right. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T19:46:15-07:00","id":1514910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514909#post1514909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that even though they're put right there in the Orders section, it's made clear that they're antagonists. The entire Seers of the Throne are given one write up instead of being split into different factions, and the write up makes it pretty clear that they're the bad guys. It's about presentation. You also can't exactly play a mixed Order game with a Seer unless something is *very* off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The point is that the Guardians police themselves. They clearly cannot be trusted to do so when their entire focus is about how they are the ones who are allowed to make the decision. &quot;I have audited myself for poor behavior and found that I was correct, case closed&quot;. Does that sound reasonable to you?<br /> It's also not really about making them &quot;seem worse&quot;, it's about pointing out how silly &quot;they're the best&quot; sounds.<br /> <br /> Actually, my argument is that killing the Friendly Neighborhood Vampire is how a Cheiron Field Projects Division agent is likely to <b><i>do evil</i></b> in the world. Yes, most of the time even Cheiron will be going after the villainous monsters, because those are the ones most easily spotted. But they're also likely to go after the safer option, which means the nice guy vampire who doesn't have a thousand kills and only feeds on drug dealers. Cheiron in particular is likely going to be on the lookout for those kind of easy to bag monsters. They aren't looking for the thrill of the hunt, they don't want to go after Alucard, they want to go after the Potency 1 Horror that lives in the sewer and scares gangbangers away from giving drugs to kids.<br /> The reason it's impossible to play a Hunter working for the Cheiron Group that isn't a baby eating monster is because the Cheiron Group is a group of baby eating monsters. Just because they don't send you, personally, to always go after the baby monsters doesn't mean it isn't on the list of things they want you to do. Hell, I've actually got the outline of a story for a Dragonslayer Knight (Order of Saint George) who falls for a wizard and realizes that he can't put it off anymore and her number is up, and how he reacts to that.<br /> <br /> No, every antagonist will not be the nice vegetarian vampire or woobie changelings. Again, that isn't the point. The point is that <i><b>as a faction</b></i> they don't give a shit. That is baked into their write ups. Meanwhile there are plenty of factions who realize that vampires and witches and faeries and ghostwalkers <i><b>are all still rational, thinking beings</b></i>. So the competing notion of &quot;every Hunter org has to be evil because that's the game you're playing&quot; also doesn't sit right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you willingly not understand? They ARE watched. Literally all other Orders dislike and distrust them. They keep each other in order and are kept in line by the other Orders. You DO realize that they aren't unique in policing right? In fact they are usually subservient. You don't seem to understand this.<br /> <br /> Plenty of factions in game lines &quot;don't give a shit&quot;. One thing you need to realize is despite that, the individuals that make up the organizations DO give a shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T20:06:04-07:00","id":1514911,"title":"","content":"I don't think you understand why &quot;they police themselves&quot; in this case is worse than the other organizations that do the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T20:12:17-07:00","id":1514912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1504062-so-i-m-currently-reading-the-2nd-edition?p=1514911#post1514911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you understand why &quot;they police themselves&quot; in this case is worse than the other organizations that do the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit. They police themselves and are placed, PURPOSELY BY THEIR OWN SYMBOLISM, under scrutiny by all other Orders. And they are VERY necessary Order without considering that.<br /> <br /> im getting the feeling you have emotional or political reasons not to like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 06-13-2023, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T20:52:21-07:00","id":1514914,"title":"","content":"Swinging this back around to the intended topic (because debating morality in Mage is something best kept to the table, IMO), is this all about the morality of Hunter Orgs on the Macro scale, or the Cell scale? Because you can absolutely run a Charon cell as:<br /> <br /> &quot;Echo squad, we have a new target. Confirmed bloodsucker, with multiple enthralled victims identified. Terminate with extreme predjudice, but remember to keep it intact enough for us to keep getting funded. Ammo ain't cheap.&quot;<br /> <br /> The organization may be evil overall, but that doesnt mean the cell has to be, any more than the average employee in a Nestl\u00e9 factory is.<br /> <br /> To the average Hunter, the supernaturals they hunt are <i>threats</i>. And they're far from wrong. There's a reason monster-affiliated Cells have the moniker of &quot;Cancer Cell&quot;.<br /> <br /> Plus, (and this is my favorite part) <i>going rogue is an option</i>. Just because you started working for Charon doesn't mean you have to <i>keep</i> doing so, if presented alternatives. And honestly, what better way to wrap up a campaign than declaring war on the greater evil?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 06-13-2023, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T08:43:23-07:00","id":1514959,"title":"","content":"That's a good point about the macro and cell levels.<br /> Most of the other gamelines divide up factions into the polite society default playable group (Pentacle, Covenants, etc), the much less polite but still playable if you stretch group (Seers, Belial's Brood) and then the really scary monsters (Scelesti, VII/Strix).<br /> Hunter doesn't do this, probably because the game's focus on fighting monsters is unique among the gamelines, but hunter vs hunter is explicitly supported by the game. So Hunters fight monsters, but differences in two Hunter's Codes can and do lead to deadly violence.<br /> If Hunter <i>was</i> organized that way I suspect Cheiron would absolutely be in the &quot;Less-polite playable antagonist&quot; category. Aside from being evil (they do, after all, vivisect sentient beings for occult power and profit), I think they're thematically excellent villains as well; exploiting the supernatural for selfish reasons is one of the big issues Hunters in general have with witches, per <i>Witchfinders</i>, and while most hunter conspiracies arguably exploit the trauma of their inductees to better wield them against the monsters they fight, Cheiron takes that to extremes. And while regulatory capture is something that every hunter conspiracy struggles with, Cheiron has always been run by inhuman entities using human hunters as catspaws.<br /> At the macro level they strike me as less of a &quot;hunter conspiracy&quot; and more as a &quot;conspiracy that happens to use hunters to achieve its goals&quot;, which feels like a great example of a &quot;cautionary tale&quot; sort of antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T08:19:15-07:00","id":1515538,"title":"","content":"When it comes to the degree of morality of a hunter organization, I always ask these two questions: \u00bfIs the hunt the end itself or is it the means to an end? \u00bfWhich one has the priority between protecting the innocent and hunting the monster? Let's put the Cheiron group as an example, first question: The hunt is a means to get rich, with any benefit to society as a side effect; second question: Capturing the monster is always the priority, it's their main source of revenue. Taking into account these answers, it's pretty obvious that they're not particularly moral, and that's ok, it's how they're designed. The Cheiron group represents a particular philosophy of the hunt, one motivated by profit. Ask then your players if this is something that they want to explore, \u00bfDoes the idea of playing mercenaries with monster parts implanted on them for a ruthless company sound appealing? \u00bfDo they want to explore the morality of their situation? \u00bfDo they seek to expose the organization? That said, I personally use the Cheiron group more as an antagonist faction or a temporal ally for my players. Also, I just want to emphasize that the morality of the hunters is entirely a personal matter for my players, they don't need to share the morality of their faction, but they do have to give me a justification that makes sense for why they're working for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}